{"chunk_id": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020_p0001_c0007", "source_registry_id": "src_5e577a90926d", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "56799e0003a1a200", "text_span_hash": "56799e0003a1a200", "source_file": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "page": 1, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 7, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "of anecdotal data without scientiﬁc support, while most\nscientiﬁc evidence on endurance running was developed from studies observing both recreational\nand professional athletes of diﬀerent levels. Further, the transference of all this information to", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Factors Aﬀecting Training and Physical Performance\nin Recreational Endurance Runners\n, Jonathan Esteve-Lanao 2, Arturo Casado 3\nLeonardo A. Peyré-Tartaruga 4\n, Rodrigo Gomes da Rosa 4 and Juan Del Coso 5\nGraduate Program in Movement Sciences, Federal University of Mato Grosso do Sul, Campo Grande, Mato\nGrosso do Sul 79070-900, Brazil\nAll in Your Mind Training System™, Mérida, Yucatán 97134, Mexico; jonathan.esteve@allinyourmind.es\nFaculty of Health Sciences, Isabel I de Castilla International University, Burgos, 09003 Castilla y León, Spain;\narturocasado1500@gmail.com\nExercise Research Laboratory, Universidade Federal do Rio Grande do Sul, Porto Alegre, Rio Grande do Sul\n90690-200, Brazil; leotartaruga@gmail.com (L.A.P.-T.); rodrigogomesdarosa@gmail.com (R.G.d.R.)\nCentre for Sport Studies, Rey Juan Carlos University, Fuenlabrada, 28943 Madrid, Spain; juan.delcoso@urjc.es\nAbstract: Endurance running has become an immensely popular sporting activity, with millions\nof recreational runners around the world. Despite the great popularity of endurance running as a\nrecreational activity during leisure time, there is no consensus on the best practice for recreational\nrunners to eﬀectively train to reach their individual objectives and improve physical performance in a\nhealthy manner. Moreover, there are lots of anecdotal data without scientiﬁc support, while most\nscientiﬁc evidence on endurance running was developed from studies observ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "of anecdotal data without scientiﬁc support, while most\nscientiﬁc evidence on endurance running was developed from studies observing both recreational\nand professional athletes of diﬀerent levels. Further, the transference of all this information to"}
{"chunk_id": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020_p0001_c0008", "source_registry_id": "src_5e577a90926d", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "669cbef067e5762c", "text_span_hash": "669cbef067e5762c", "source_file": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "page": 1, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 8, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "nce of all this information to\nonly recreational runners is diﬃcult due to diﬀerences in the genetic predisposition for endurance\nrunning, the time available for training, and physical, psychological, and physiological characteristics.\nTherefore, the", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Factors Aﬀecting Training and Physical Performance\nin Recreational Endurance Runners\n, Jonathan Esteve-Lanao 2, Arturo Casado 3\nLeonardo A. Peyré-Tartaruga 4\n, Rodrigo Gomes da Rosa 4 and Juan Del Coso 5\nGraduate Program in Movement Sciences, Federal University of Mato Grosso do Sul, Campo Grande, Mato\nGrosso do Sul 79070-900, Brazil\nAll in Your Mind Training System™, Mérida, Yucatán 97134, Mexico; jonathan.esteve@allinyourmind.es\nFaculty of Health Sciences, Isabel I de Castilla International University, Burgos, 09003 Castilla y León, Spain;\narturocasado1500@gmail.com\nExercise Research Laboratory, Universidade Federal do Rio Grande do Sul, Porto Alegre, Rio Grande do Sul\n90690-200, Brazil; leotartaruga@gmail.com (L.A.P.-T.); rodrigogomesdarosa@gmail.com (R.G.d.R.)\nCentre for Sport Studies, Rey Juan Carlos University, Fuenlabrada, 28943 Madrid, Spain; juan.delcoso@urjc.es\nAbstract: Endurance running has become an immensely popular sporting activity, with millions\nof recreational runners around the world. Despite the great popularity of endurance running as a\nrecreational activity during leisure time, there is no consensus on the best practice for recreational\nrunners to eﬀectively train to reach their individual objectives and improve physical performance in a\nhealthy manner. Moreover, there are lots of anecdotal data without scientiﬁc support, while most\nscientiﬁc evidence on endurance running was developed from studies observ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "nce of all this information to\nonly recreational runners is diﬃcult due to diﬀerences in the genetic predisposition for endurance\nrunning, the time available for training, and physical, psychological, and physiological characteristics.\nTherefore, the"}
{"chunk_id": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020_p0001_c0009", "source_registry_id": "src_5e577a90926d", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "0650ed0937bb9ce9", "text_span_hash": "0650ed0937bb9ce9", "source_file": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "page": 1, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 9, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "haracteristics.\nTherefore, the aim of this review is to present a selection of scientiﬁc evidence regarding endurance\nrunning to provide training guidelines to be used by recreational runners and their coaches. The review\nwill focus on some key aspec", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Factors Aﬀecting Training and Physical Performance\nin Recreational Endurance Runners\n, Jonathan Esteve-Lanao 2, Arturo Casado 3\nLeonardo A. Peyré-Tartaruga 4\n, Rodrigo Gomes da Rosa 4 and Juan Del Coso 5\nGraduate Program in Movement Sciences, Federal University of Mato Grosso do Sul, Campo Grande, Mato\nGrosso do Sul 79070-900, Brazil\nAll in Your Mind Training System™, Mérida, Yucatán 97134, Mexico; jonathan.esteve@allinyourmind.es\nFaculty of Health Sciences, Isabel I de Castilla International University, Burgos, 09003 Castilla y León, Spain;\narturocasado1500@gmail.com\nExercise Research Laboratory, Universidade Federal do Rio Grande do Sul, Porto Alegre, Rio Grande do Sul\n90690-200, Brazil; leotartaruga@gmail.com (L.A.P.-T.); rodrigogomesdarosa@gmail.com (R.G.d.R.)\nCentre for Sport Studies, Rey Juan Carlos University, Fuenlabrada, 28943 Madrid, Spain; juan.delcoso@urjc.es\nAbstract: Endurance running has become an immensely popular sporting activity, with millions\nof recreational runners around the world. Despite the great popularity of endurance running as a\nrecreational activity during leisure time, there is no consensus on the best practice for recreational\nrunners to eﬀectively train to reach their individual objectives and improve physical performance in a\nhealthy manner. Moreover, there are lots of anecdotal data without scientiﬁc support, while most\nscientiﬁc evidence on endurance running was developed from studies observ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "haracteristics.\nTherefore, the aim of this review is to present a selection of scientiﬁc evidence regarding endurance\nrunning to provide training guidelines to be used by recreational runners and their coaches. The review\nwill focus on some key aspec"}
{"chunk_id": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020_p0001_c0010", "source_registry_id": "src_5e577a90926d", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "4be0afe8f18069ca", "text_span_hash": "4be0afe8f18069ca", "source_file": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "page": 1, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 10, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "w\nwill focus on some key aspects of the training process, such as periodization, training methods and\nmonitoring, performance prediction, running technique, and prevention and management of injuries\nassociated with endurance running.\nKeywords: endura", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Factors Aﬀecting Training and Physical Performance\nin Recreational Endurance Runners\n, Jonathan Esteve-Lanao 2, Arturo Casado 3\nLeonardo A. Peyré-Tartaruga 4\n, Rodrigo Gomes da Rosa 4 and Juan Del Coso 5\nGraduate Program in Movement Sciences, Federal University of Mato Grosso do Sul, Campo Grande, Mato\nGrosso do Sul 79070-900, Brazil\nAll in Your Mind Training System™, Mérida, Yucatán 97134, Mexico; jonathan.esteve@allinyourmind.es\nFaculty of Health Sciences, Isabel I de Castilla International University, Burgos, 09003 Castilla y León, Spain;\narturocasado1500@gmail.com\nExercise Research Laboratory, Universidade Federal do Rio Grande do Sul, Porto Alegre, Rio Grande do Sul\n90690-200, Brazil; leotartaruga@gmail.com (L.A.P.-T.); rodrigogomesdarosa@gmail.com (R.G.d.R.)\nCentre for Sport Studies, Rey Juan Carlos University, Fuenlabrada, 28943 Madrid, Spain; juan.delcoso@urjc.es\nAbstract: Endurance running has become an immensely popular sporting activity, with millions\nof recreational runners around the world. Despite the great popularity of endurance running as a\nrecreational activity during leisure time, there is no consensus on the best practice for recreational\nrunners to eﬀectively train to reach their individual objectives and improve physical performance in a\nhealthy manner. Moreover, there are lots of anecdotal data without scientiﬁc support, while most\nscientiﬁc evidence on endurance running was developed from studies observ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "w\nwill focus on some key aspects of the training process, such as periodization, training methods and\nmonitoring, performance prediction, running technique, and prevention and management of injuries\nassociated with endurance running.\nKeywords: endura"}
{"chunk_id": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020_p0001_c0011", "source_registry_id": "src_5e577a90926d", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "70a162ec9cd18385", "text_span_hash": "70a162ec9cd18385", "source_file": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "page": 1, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 11, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "ance running.\nKeywords: endurance exercise; sports performance; sports training; running technique; exercise\nintensity; amateur runner\nEndurance running has been suggested to be a biological trait associated with the survival\nof our species [1,2]. In", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Factors Aﬀecting Training and Physical Performance\nin Recreational Endurance Runners\n, Jonathan Esteve-Lanao 2, Arturo Casado 3\nLeonardo A. Peyré-Tartaruga 4\n, Rodrigo Gomes da Rosa 4 and Juan Del Coso 5\nGraduate Program in Movement Sciences, Federal University of Mato Grosso do Sul, Campo Grande, Mato\nGrosso do Sul 79070-900, Brazil\nAll in Your Mind Training System™, Mérida, Yucatán 97134, Mexico; jonathan.esteve@allinyourmind.es\nFaculty of Health Sciences, Isabel I de Castilla International University, Burgos, 09003 Castilla y León, Spain;\narturocasado1500@gmail.com\nExercise Research Laboratory, Universidade Federal do Rio Grande do Sul, Porto Alegre, Rio Grande do Sul\n90690-200, Brazil; leotartaruga@gmail.com (L.A.P.-T.); rodrigogomesdarosa@gmail.com (R.G.d.R.)\nCentre for Sport Studies, Rey Juan Carlos University, Fuenlabrada, 28943 Madrid, Spain; juan.delcoso@urjc.es\nAbstract: Endurance running has become an immensely popular sporting activity, with millions\nof recreational runners around the world. Despite the great popularity of endurance running as a\nrecreational activity during leisure time, there is no consensus on the best practice for recreational\nrunners to eﬀectively train to reach their individual objectives and improve physical performance in a\nhealthy manner. Moreover, there are lots of anecdotal data without scientiﬁc support, while most\nscientiﬁc evidence on endurance running was developed from studies observ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "ance running.\nKeywords: endurance exercise; sports performance; sports training; running technique; exercise\nintensity; amateur runner\nEndurance running has been suggested to be a biological trait associated with the survival\nof our species [1,2]. In"}
{"chunk_id": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020_p0001_c0012", "source_registry_id": "src_5e577a90926d", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "0997472b71d3176f", "text_span_hash": "0997472b71d3176f", "source_file": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "page": 1, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 12, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "vival\nof our species [1,2]. In fact, our species could be considered one of the best examples of natural\nendurance athletes, with neurobiological mechanisms reinforcing the search for habitual aerobic\nexercise, particularly running [3]. Therefore, it", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Factors Aﬀecting Training and Physical Performance\nin Recreational Endurance Runners\n, Jonathan Esteve-Lanao 2, Arturo Casado 3\nLeonardo A. Peyré-Tartaruga 4\n, Rodrigo Gomes da Rosa 4 and Juan Del Coso 5\nGraduate Program in Movement Sciences, Federal University of Mato Grosso do Sul, Campo Grande, Mato\nGrosso do Sul 79070-900, Brazil\nAll in Your Mind Training System™, Mérida, Yucatán 97134, Mexico; jonathan.esteve@allinyourmind.es\nFaculty of Health Sciences, Isabel I de Castilla International University, Burgos, 09003 Castilla y León, Spain;\narturocasado1500@gmail.com\nExercise Research Laboratory, Universidade Federal do Rio Grande do Sul, Porto Alegre, Rio Grande do Sul\n90690-200, Brazil; leotartaruga@gmail.com (L.A.P.-T.); rodrigogomesdarosa@gmail.com (R.G.d.R.)\nCentre for Sport Studies, Rey Juan Carlos University, Fuenlabrada, 28943 Madrid, Spain; juan.delcoso@urjc.es\nAbstract: Endurance running has become an immensely popular sporting activity, with millions\nof recreational runners around the world. Despite the great popularity of endurance running as a\nrecreational activity during leisure time, there is no consensus on the best practice for recreational\nrunners to eﬀectively train to reach their individual objectives and improve physical performance in a\nhealthy manner. Moreover, there are lots of anecdotal data without scientiﬁc support, while most\nscientiﬁc evidence on endurance running was developed from studies observ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "vival\nof our species [1,2]. In fact, our species could be considered one of the best examples of natural\nendurance athletes, with neurobiological mechanisms reinforcing the search for habitual aerobic\nexercise, particularly running [3]. Therefore, it"}
{"chunk_id": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020_p0001_c0013", "source_registry_id": "src_5e577a90926d", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "752a47e62dd370bc", "text_span_hash": "752a47e62dd370bc", "source_file": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "page": 1, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 13, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "rly running [3]. Therefore, it is easy to understand why millions of people compete\nevery weekend in road endurance running races of variable distances, from 5 km to marathon races,\naround the world [4,5]. Currently, a great number of recreational ru", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Factors Aﬀecting Training and Physical Performance\nin Recreational Endurance Runners\n, Jonathan Esteve-Lanao 2, Arturo Casado 3\nLeonardo A. Peyré-Tartaruga 4\n, Rodrigo Gomes da Rosa 4 and Juan Del Coso 5\nGraduate Program in Movement Sciences, Federal University of Mato Grosso do Sul, Campo Grande, Mato\nGrosso do Sul 79070-900, Brazil\nAll in Your Mind Training System™, Mérida, Yucatán 97134, Mexico; jonathan.esteve@allinyourmind.es\nFaculty of Health Sciences, Isabel I de Castilla International University, Burgos, 09003 Castilla y León, Spain;\narturocasado1500@gmail.com\nExercise Research Laboratory, Universidade Federal do Rio Grande do Sul, Porto Alegre, Rio Grande do Sul\n90690-200, Brazil; leotartaruga@gmail.com (L.A.P.-T.); rodrigogomesdarosa@gmail.com (R.G.d.R.)\nCentre for Sport Studies, Rey Juan Carlos University, Fuenlabrada, 28943 Madrid, Spain; juan.delcoso@urjc.es\nAbstract: Endurance running has become an immensely popular sporting activity, with millions\nof recreational runners around the world. Despite the great popularity of endurance running as a\nrecreational activity during leisure time, there is no consensus on the best practice for recreational\nrunners to eﬀectively train to reach their individual objectives and improve physical performance in a\nhealthy manner. Moreover, there are lots of anecdotal data without scientiﬁc support, while most\nscientiﬁc evidence on endurance running was developed from studies observ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "rly running [3]. Therefore, it is easy to understand why millions of people compete\nevery weekend in road endurance running races of variable distances, from 5 km to marathon races,\naround the world [4,5]. Currently, a great number of recreational ru"}
{"chunk_id": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020_p0001_c0014", "source_registry_id": "src_5e577a90926d", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "67498e621d799f75", "text_span_hash": "67498e621d799f75", "source_file": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "page": 1, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 14, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "reat number of recreational runners train every day in diﬀerent\nplaces. The success of this recreational sport might be attributed to its simplicity and accessibility\nwhile favoring health development [6], and the social interactions and leisure expe", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Factors Aﬀecting Training and Physical Performance\nin Recreational Endurance Runners\n, Jonathan Esteve-Lanao 2, Arturo Casado 3\nLeonardo A. Peyré-Tartaruga 4\n, Rodrigo Gomes da Rosa 4 and Juan Del Coso 5\nGraduate Program in Movement Sciences, Federal University of Mato Grosso do Sul, Campo Grande, Mato\nGrosso do Sul 79070-900, Brazil\nAll in Your Mind Training System™, Mérida, Yucatán 97134, Mexico; jonathan.esteve@allinyourmind.es\nFaculty of Health Sciences, Isabel I de Castilla International University, Burgos, 09003 Castilla y León, Spain;\narturocasado1500@gmail.com\nExercise Research Laboratory, Universidade Federal do Rio Grande do Sul, Porto Alegre, Rio Grande do Sul\n90690-200, Brazil; leotartaruga@gmail.com (L.A.P.-T.); rodrigogomesdarosa@gmail.com (R.G.d.R.)\nCentre for Sport Studies, Rey Juan Carlos University, Fuenlabrada, 28943 Madrid, Spain; juan.delcoso@urjc.es\nAbstract: Endurance running has become an immensely popular sporting activity, with millions\nof recreational runners around the world. Despite the great popularity of endurance running as a\nrecreational activity during leisure time, there is no consensus on the best practice for recreational\nrunners to eﬀectively train to reach their individual objectives and improve physical performance in a\nhealthy manner. Moreover, there are lots of anecdotal data without scientiﬁc support, while most\nscientiﬁc evidence on endurance running was developed from studies observ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "reat number of recreational runners train every day in diﬀerent\nplaces. The success of this recreational sport might be attributed to its simplicity and accessibility\nwhile favoring health development [6], and the social interactions and leisure expe"}
{"chunk_id": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020_p0001_c0015", "source_registry_id": "src_5e577a90926d", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "67b6bd41fdbb77ab", "text_span_hash": "67b6bd41fdbb77ab", "source_file": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "page": 1, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 15, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "interactions and leisure experiences that it lends\nto most people, regardless of level or age.\nDespite its great popularity, there is no consensus on the best practice when looking for sustained\nor improved endurance running performance in recreatio", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Factors Aﬀecting Training and Physical Performance\nin Recreational Endurance Runners\n, Jonathan Esteve-Lanao 2, Arturo Casado 3\nLeonardo A. Peyré-Tartaruga 4\n, Rodrigo Gomes da Rosa 4 and Juan Del Coso 5\nGraduate Program in Movement Sciences, Federal University of Mato Grosso do Sul, Campo Grande, Mato\nGrosso do Sul 79070-900, Brazil\nAll in Your Mind Training System™, Mérida, Yucatán 97134, Mexico; jonathan.esteve@allinyourmind.es\nFaculty of Health Sciences, Isabel I de Castilla International University, Burgos, 09003 Castilla y León, Spain;\narturocasado1500@gmail.com\nExercise Research Laboratory, Universidade Federal do Rio Grande do Sul, Porto Alegre, Rio Grande do Sul\n90690-200, Brazil; leotartaruga@gmail.com (L.A.P.-T.); rodrigogomesdarosa@gmail.com (R.G.d.R.)\nCentre for Sport Studies, Rey Juan Carlos University, Fuenlabrada, 28943 Madrid, Spain; juan.delcoso@urjc.es\nAbstract: Endurance running has become an immensely popular sporting activity, with millions\nof recreational runners around the world. Despite the great popularity of endurance running as a\nrecreational activity during leisure time, there is no consensus on the best practice for recreational\nrunners to eﬀectively train to reach their individual objectives and improve physical performance in a\nhealthy manner. Moreover, there are lots of anecdotal data without scientiﬁc support, while most\nscientiﬁc evidence on endurance running was developed from studies observ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "interactions and leisure experiences that it lends\nto most people, regardless of level or age.\nDespite its great popularity, there is no consensus on the best practice when looking for sustained\nor improved endurance running performance in recreatio"}
{"chunk_id": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020_p0001_c0016", "source_registry_id": "src_5e577a90926d", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "dde47f28797b4672", "text_span_hash": "dde47f28797b4672", "source_file": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "page": 1, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 16, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "nning performance in recreational running while maintaining or enhancing\nwww.mdpi.com/journal/sports", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Factors Aﬀecting Training and Physical Performance\nin Recreational Endurance Runners\n, Jonathan Esteve-Lanao 2, Arturo Casado 3\nLeonardo A. Peyré-Tartaruga 4\n, Rodrigo Gomes da Rosa 4 and Juan Del Coso 5\nGraduate Program in Movement Sciences, Federal University of Mato Grosso do Sul, Campo Grande, Mato\nGrosso do Sul 79070-900, Brazil\nAll in Your Mind Training System™, Mérida, Yucatán 97134, Mexico; jonathan.esteve@allinyourmind.es\nFaculty of Health Sciences, Isabel I de Castilla International University, Burgos, 09003 Castilla y León, Spain;\narturocasado1500@gmail.com\nExercise Research Laboratory, Universidade Federal do Rio Grande do Sul, Porto Alegre, Rio Grande do Sul\n90690-200, Brazil; leotartaruga@gmail.com (L.A.P.-T.); rodrigogomesdarosa@gmail.com (R.G.d.R.)\nCentre for Sport Studies, Rey Juan Carlos University, Fuenlabrada, 28943 Madrid, Spain; juan.delcoso@urjc.es\nAbstract: Endurance running has become an immensely popular sporting activity, with millions\nof recreational runners around the world. Despite the great popularity of endurance running as a\nrecreational activity during leisure time, there is no consensus on the best practice for recreational\nrunners to eﬀectively train to reach their individual objectives and improve physical performance in a\nhealthy manner. Moreover, there are lots of anecdotal data without scientiﬁc support, while most\nscientiﬁc evidence on endurance running was developed from studies observ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "nning performance in recreational running while maintaining or enhancing\nwww.mdpi.com/journal/sports"}
{"chunk_id": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020_p0002_c0001", "source_registry_id": "src_5e577a90926d", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "ff755df0d33c215b", "text_span_hash": "ff755df0d33c215b", "source_file": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "page": 2, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 1, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "health status. However, there are a plethora of anecdotal guidelines without robust scientiﬁc support,\nincluding the use of nonvalidated algorithms (e.g., Trainingpeaks™) for training monitoring, the\n“10% rule” for weekly training load increments, or", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "health status. However, there are a plethora of anecdotal guidelines without robust scientiﬁc support,\nincluding the use of nonvalidated algorithms (e.g., Trainingpeaks™) for training monitoring, the\n“10% rule” for weekly training load increments, or the use of diﬀerent types of shoes to reduce injury\nrates. In fact, it is common to see recreational runners imitating training practices similar to those\nof professional athletes, including completion of high weekly mileage (e.g., > 70 km), which may be\nbehind the high prevalence of some health-related problems [7]. Further, as current scientiﬁc evidence\non endurance running was developed from studies observing recreational and professional athletes of\nvery diﬀerent levels (from untrained to elite), it is unclear how recreational runners can eﬀectively use\nall the available information. Furthermore, the deﬁnition of a recreational runner is very wide, since\nwe could include in this category any runner who trains and competes regularly during leisure time\nindependently of the performance level (from novice to well-trained athletes) and speciﬁc objectives\n(e.g., enjoyment, health, competition, etc.). However, in contrast to professional athletes, recreational\nrunners have limited schedules to train, which often are adapted to other daily living activities and\nduties. Moreover, although some ex-professional athletes exist in the recreational runner category, it\nis expected that most", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "health status. However, there are a plethora of anecdotal guidelines without robust scientiﬁc support,\nincluding the use of nonvalidated algorithms (e.g., Trainingpeaks™) for training monitoring, the\n“10% rule” for weekly training load increments, or"}
{"chunk_id": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020_p0002_c0003", "source_registry_id": "src_5e577a90926d", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "8e42c7bbc35d51f6", "text_span_hash": "8e42c7bbc35d51f6", "source_file": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "page": 2, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 3, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "g completion of high weekly mileage (e.g., > 70 km), which may be\nbehind the high prevalence of some health-related problems [7]. Further, as current scientiﬁc evidence\non endurance running was developed from studies observing recreational and profes", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "health status. However, there are a plethora of anecdotal guidelines without robust scientiﬁc support,\nincluding the use of nonvalidated algorithms (e.g., Trainingpeaks™) for training monitoring, the\n“10% rule” for weekly training load increments, or the use of diﬀerent types of shoes to reduce injury\nrates. In fact, it is common to see recreational runners imitating training practices similar to those\nof professional athletes, including completion of high weekly mileage (e.g., > 70 km), which may be\nbehind the high prevalence of some health-related problems [7]. Further, as current scientiﬁc evidence\non endurance running was developed from studies observing recreational and professional athletes of\nvery diﬀerent levels (from untrained to elite), it is unclear how recreational runners can eﬀectively use\nall the available information. Furthermore, the deﬁnition of a recreational runner is very wide, since\nwe could include in this category any runner who trains and competes regularly during leisure time\nindependently of the performance level (from novice to well-trained athletes) and speciﬁc objectives\n(e.g., enjoyment, health, competition, etc.). However, in contrast to professional athletes, recreational\nrunners have limited schedules to train, which often are adapted to other daily living activities and\nduties. Moreover, although some ex-professional athletes exist in the recreational runner category, it\nis expected that most", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "g completion of high weekly mileage (e.g., > 70 km), which may be\nbehind the high prevalence of some health-related problems [7]. Further, as current scientiﬁc evidence\non endurance running was developed from studies observing recreational and profes"}
{"chunk_id": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020_p0002_c0004", "source_registry_id": "src_5e577a90926d", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "851d79873e6c0992", "text_span_hash": "851d79873e6c0992", "source_file": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "page": 2, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 4, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "erving recreational and professional athletes of\nvery diﬀerent levels (from untrained to elite), it is unclear how recreational runners can eﬀectively use\nall the available information. Furthermore, the deﬁnition of a recreational runner is very wide", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "health status. However, there are a plethora of anecdotal guidelines without robust scientiﬁc support,\nincluding the use of nonvalidated algorithms (e.g., Trainingpeaks™) for training monitoring, the\n“10% rule” for weekly training load increments, or the use of diﬀerent types of shoes to reduce injury\nrates. In fact, it is common to see recreational runners imitating training practices similar to those\nof professional athletes, including completion of high weekly mileage (e.g., > 70 km), which may be\nbehind the high prevalence of some health-related problems [7]. Further, as current scientiﬁc evidence\non endurance running was developed from studies observing recreational and professional athletes of\nvery diﬀerent levels (from untrained to elite), it is unclear how recreational runners can eﬀectively use\nall the available information. Furthermore, the deﬁnition of a recreational runner is very wide, since\nwe could include in this category any runner who trains and competes regularly during leisure time\nindependently of the performance level (from novice to well-trained athletes) and speciﬁc objectives\n(e.g., enjoyment, health, competition, etc.). However, in contrast to professional athletes, recreational\nrunners have limited schedules to train, which often are adapted to other daily living activities and\nduties. Moreover, although some ex-professional athletes exist in the recreational runner category, it\nis expected that most", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "erving recreational and professional athletes of\nvery diﬀerent levels (from untrained to elite), it is unclear how recreational runners can eﬀectively use\nall the available information. Furthermore, the deﬁnition of a recreational runner is very wide"}
{"chunk_id": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020_p0002_c0005", "source_registry_id": "src_5e577a90926d", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "c47225e571ae28af", "text_span_hash": "c47225e571ae28af", "source_file": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "page": 2, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 5, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "creational runner is very wide, since\nwe could include in this category any runner who trains and competes regularly during leisure time\nindependently of the performance level (from novice to well-trained athletes) and speciﬁc objectives\n(e.g., enjoy", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "health status. However, there are a plethora of anecdotal guidelines without robust scientiﬁc support,\nincluding the use of nonvalidated algorithms (e.g., Trainingpeaks™) for training monitoring, the\n“10% rule” for weekly training load increments, or the use of diﬀerent types of shoes to reduce injury\nrates. In fact, it is common to see recreational runners imitating training practices similar to those\nof professional athletes, including completion of high weekly mileage (e.g., > 70 km), which may be\nbehind the high prevalence of some health-related problems [7]. Further, as current scientiﬁc evidence\non endurance running was developed from studies observing recreational and professional athletes of\nvery diﬀerent levels (from untrained to elite), it is unclear how recreational runners can eﬀectively use\nall the available information. Furthermore, the deﬁnition of a recreational runner is very wide, since\nwe could include in this category any runner who trains and competes regularly during leisure time\nindependently of the performance level (from novice to well-trained athletes) and speciﬁc objectives\n(e.g., enjoyment, health, competition, etc.). However, in contrast to professional athletes, recreational\nrunners have limited schedules to train, which often are adapted to other daily living activities and\nduties. Moreover, although some ex-professional athletes exist in the recreational runner category, it\nis expected that most", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "creational runner is very wide, since\nwe could include in this category any runner who trains and competes regularly during leisure time\nindependently of the performance level (from novice to well-trained athletes) and speciﬁc objectives\n(e.g., enjoy"}
{"chunk_id": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020_p0002_c0006", "source_registry_id": "src_5e577a90926d", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "bb0704badbc2c8ed", "text_span_hash": "bb0704badbc2c8ed", "source_file": "1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\1_recreational_runners_factors_2020.pdf", "page": 2, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 6, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "peciﬁc objectives\n(e.g., enjoyment, health, competition, etc.). However, in contrast to professional athletes, recreational\nrunners have limited schedules to train, which often are adapted to other daily living activities and\nduties. Moreover, althou", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "health status. However, there are a plethora of anecdotal guidelines without robust scientiﬁc support,\nincluding the use of nonvalidated algorithms (e.g., Trainingpeaks™) for training monitoring, the\n“10% rule” for weekly training load increments, or the use of diﬀerent types of shoes to reduce injury\nrates. In fact, it is common to see recreational runners imitating training practices similar to those\nof professional athletes, including completion of high weekly mileage (e.g., > 70 km), which may be\nbehind the high prevalence of some health-related problems [7]. Further, as current scientiﬁc evidence\non endurance running was developed from studies observing recreational and professional athletes of\nvery diﬀerent levels (from untrained to elite), it is unclear how recreational runners can eﬀectively use\nall the available information. Furthermore, the deﬁnition of a recreational runner is very wide, since\nwe could include in this category any runner who trains and competes regularly during leisure time\nindependently of the performance level (from novice to well-trained athletes) and speciﬁc objectives\n(e.g., enjoyment, health, competitio