bility. Thus, other low-cost and simple evaluations could be used, especially\nin the ﬁeld. From these tests, incremental ﬁeld-testing for identiﬁcation of maximum aerobic speed\n(MAS) could be considered the most practical, as MAS integrates both VO2max and RE into a single\nparameter and was used", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "sting sessions and competitions should be also included in TID calculations [46].\nIn addition, the minimum running volume required to improve running performance in recreational\nrunners [47], including the interactions between TID, running, and ST me"}
