ability. Thus, other low-cost and simple evaluations could be used, especially\nin the ﬁeld. From these tests, incremental ﬁeld-testing for identiﬁcation of maximum aerobic speed\n(MAS) could be considered the most practical, as MAS integrates both VO2max and RE into a single\nparameter and was used", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "etween TID, running, and ST methods [48] and the signiﬁcant\ninﬂuence of incidental physical activity on running training adaptations [49] still require identiﬁcation.\n3. Training Monitoring\nRecreational runners can monitor their progress through seve"}
