bility. Thus, other low-cost and simple evaluations could be used, especially\nin the ﬁeld. From these tests, incremental ﬁeld-testing for identiﬁcation of maximum aerobic speed\n(MAS) could be considered the most practical, as MAS integrates both VO2max and RE into a single\nparameter and was used", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "or their progress through several traditional and modern parameters\nobtained from training and testing sessions, or competitions. Namely, traditional laboratory evaluations\naiming to identify changes in gold standard physiological measures, such as V"}
