on deﬁciency anemia, which presents the\nmost severe form of iron status abnormalities characterized by hemoglobin con-\ncentrations below the clinical range of 130 g/L in males and 120 g/L in female, is\nsimilar among athletes and general population, the prevalence of iron depletion,\ncharacterized by low i", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "s is further elevated due to the iron loss of\nmenstrual bleeding, and the prevalence of iron depletion in female athletes can be as\nhigh as 37 %, which is approximately 1.5 times greater than in sedentary women\nFor endurance athletes, it is typically"}
