on deﬁciency anemia, which presents the\nmost severe form of iron status abnormalities characterized by hemoglobin con-\ncentrations below the clinical range of 130 g/L in males and 120 g/L in female, is\nsimilar among athletes and general population, the prevalence of iron depletion,\ncharacterized by low i", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "ance athletes, it is typically recommended to monitor iron status at\nregular intervals of 1–2 times per year (Rodriguez et al. 2009). Clinical measures of\niron status (Table 3.1) include makers of iron storage, such as ferritin, markers of\ncellular i"}
