ning volume from\nzone 1 (at or below speed at ﬁrst ventilatory/lactate threshold [LT]) to zone 2 (between speeds associated with either both\nventilatory thresholds or 2 and 4 mmol·L−1 LTs [vLT1 and vLT2, respectively]) and zone 3 (speed above vVT2/vLT2).\nContinuous-tempo runs or interval t", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "2, respectively). Zone 3 (z3) represents speeds above VT2/\nvLT2.12 In order to analyze the effect of particular combinations of\ntraining volume and intensity in each of these zones, different TID\nmodels have been described.\n1. The pyramidal model is"}
