ining volume from\nzone 1 (at or below speed at ﬁrst ventilatory/lactate threshold [LT]) to zone 2 (between speeds associated with either both\nventilatory thresholds or 2 and 4 mmol·L−1 LTs [vLT1 and vLT2, respectively]) and zone 3 (speed above vVT2/vLT2).\nContinuous-tempo runs or interval t", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "of accumulating\nthe majority of the training volume (ie, 60%–62%) in z1.\nHowever, these delimitations have not yet reached a full consensus\nin the current literature and therefore further discussion on this\ntopic is encouraged. A recent review, exami"}
