 elite middle- and long-distance\nrunners.30–32,34 In addition, the use of this approach was found\nto be associated with either high levels23,31,34 or an improvement in\nRE.27,28 Some studies also reported either an increase in,27–29,33 or\nwere associated, with high levels of vVO2max.23,30,34 A few", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "zone deﬁned by physiological tests23 and weekly running distance\nfor each runner during 2 precompetitive weeks. Comparisons\nbetween 1500-m runners and marathoners TID and training volume\nwere conducted using Cohen d effect sizes24 and considered to b"}
