{"chunk_id": "2_elite_periodization_casado_2022_p0007_c0001", "source_registry_id": "src_df9ead131193", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "4e835400f609fc18", "text_span_hash": "4e835400f609fc18", "source_file": "2_elite_periodization_casado_2022.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\2_elite_periodization_casado_2022.pdf", "page": 7, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 1, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "Training methods (those\ndescribed in the studies)\nPyramidal (87%, 8%, and 5% of\ntotal training volume were per-\nformed at z1, z2, and z3, respec-\ntively) and polarized (87%, 6%, and\n7% of total training volume were\nperformed at z1, z2, and z3,\nrespec", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Training methods (those\ndescribed in the studies)\nPyramidal (87%, 8%, and 5% of\ntotal training volume were per-\nformed at z1, z2, and z3, respec-\ntively) and polarized (87%, 6%, and\n7% of total training volume were\nperformed at z1, z2, and z3,\nrespectively) during the whole sea-\nson and competitive phase, respec-\nwhole season and competitive\nA typical training week conducted\nduring the preparatory period con-\nsisted of 30–60 min easy runs at z1,\none long-run around 105 min at z1,\none tempo run (9 km) per week at\nvLT2 in z2, one hilly 7.2 km run at\nvLT2 in z2 and one anaerobic\ninterval training session at z3\n(8 × 1000 m, with 60 s of recovery).\nThese 2 last sessions were substi-\ntuted during the competitive period\nfor one short-interval training ses-\nsion on hills at z3 (6 × 800 m at 5 km\npace) and an anaerobic interval\ntraining session at z3 (4 × 1600 m\n[2-min rest] at 10 km pace,\nPyramidal during most of the season\nbut more polarized oriented during\nthe competitive period. 79 (31.33)\nkm·wk−1 in the preparatory period\ncompetitive period. 69%, z2. 17%,\nz3: 14% of the total training volume\nwere performed in z1, z2, and z3,\nTraditional periodization. Two\nmacrocycles of 6 mo each.\nVolume: always 85 −90 km·wk−1;\npreintervention: HVLI; ﬁrst period:\npyramidal approach; second period:\npolarized approach adding more\nFirst period: 4 sessions in z1 (ie, 45–\n60 min of easy run at 60%–70% of\nVO2max), 1 session at vLT2\n(ie, 2 × 20 min at 85", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "Training methods (those\ndescribed in the studies)\nPyramidal (87%, 8%, and 5% of\ntotal training volume were per-\nformed at z1, z2, and z3, respec-\ntively) and polarized (87%, 6%, and\n7% of total training volume were\nperformed at z1, z2, and z3,\nrespec"}
