nthe number of motor units recruited without the consequences of\nelevated levels of catecholamines likely to be experienced with z3\nFurthermore, speciﬁc training characteristics in highly trained\nand elite distance runners appear to inﬂuence performance and\nphysiological determinants globally. For e", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "ning (z1) with high-\nintensity training in these runners (z2 + z3) is very important\n(Figure 2D). This speciﬁc training characteristic may be related\nto a more rapid recovery of the autonomic nervous system and\nhormonal balance from one session to an"}
