search question, is rather which is\nthe most effective combination of methods to improve perfor-\nmance and its physiological determinants according to the\nspeciﬁc athlete and competitive goal. Within these different\ncombinations observed, interval training methods typically\nwere conducted at z3 and ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "highly trained and elite distance runners.\nFirst, this is the ﬁrst study attempting to differentiate TID among\ndifferent running events (ie, distances). The most important\nﬁnding is that while a polarized approach is typically followed\nby specialists"}
{"chunk_id": "2_elite_periodization_casado_2022_p0012_c0013", "source_registry_id": "src_df9ead131193", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "d561df0b62603565", "text_span_hash": "d561df0b62603565", "source_file": "2_elite_periodization_casado_2022.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\2_elite_periodization_casado_2022.pdf", "page": 12, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 13, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "ically followed\nby specialists belonging to short events such as 1500-m runners,\nas they tend to cover a greater amount of training volume in z3, a\npyramidal approach is usually adopted by those from longer\nevents such as marathon, as they accumulate", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "The most important consideration derived from the examination\nof the training methods used by highly trained and elite distance\nrunners is that rather than focusing on a single interval training\nmode, the use of several types involving differences in overall\nvolume, number of repetitions and intensity was observed.\nFor example, during a typical training week runners may con-\nduct 2 (or more) different interval training sessions covered at\nvLT2 and vVO2max, respectively.23,29–32,34 More speciﬁcally, at\nleast one continuous or medium/long aerobic interval training\nsession at vLT2/z2, and one anaerobic/short interval training\nsession in z3 per week is required to develop performance\noptimally in highly trained and elite runners.23,27,29,31,34 Elite\nrunners used to increase the number of either vLT2 or z3 sessions\nto adopt either a pyramidal or polarized approach, respectively.\nHowever, most of the current studies examining interval training\nmethods have focused on detecting which of those yields\ngreater improvements on performance, VO2max, and other\nphysiological endurance performance determinants.52 In this\nsense, maybe the correct research question, is rather which is\nthe most effective combination of methods to improve perfor-\nmance and its physiological determinants according to the\nspeciﬁc athlete and competitive goal. Within these different\ncombinations observed, interval training methods typically\nwere conducted at z3 and ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "ically followed\nby specialists belonging to short events such as 1500-m runners,\nas they tend to cover a greater amount of training volume in z3, a\npyramidal approach is usually adopted by those from longer\nevents such as marathon, as they accumulate"}
{"chunk_id": "2_elite_periodization_casado_2022_p0012_c0014", "source_registry_id": "src_df9ead131193", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "42bf587dcb46efd2", "text_span_hash": "42bf587dcb46efd2", "source_file": "2_elite_periodization_casado_2022.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\2_elite_periodization_casado_2022.pdf", "page": 12, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 14, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "s marathon, as they accumulate longer distances at,\nor close to, vLT2 pace. Second, this systematic review has\nexamined a very recent article,29 which for the ﬁrst time demon-\nstrated through a 4-armed paralleled control trial that a periodi-\nzation", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "The most important consideration derived from the examination\nof the training methods used by highly trained and elite distance\nrunners is that rather than focusing on a single interval training\nmode, the use of several types involving differences in overall\nvolume, number of repetitions and intensity was observed.\nFor example, during a typical training week runners may con-\nduct 2 (or more) different interval training sessions covered at\nvLT2 and vVO2max, respectively.23,29–32,34 More speciﬁcally, at\nleast one continuous or medium/long aerobic interval training\nsession at vLT2/z2, and one anaerobic/short interval training\nsession in z3 per week is required to develop performance\noptimally in highly trained and elite runners.23,27,29,31,34 Elite\nrunners used to increase the number of either vLT2 or z3 sessions\nto adopt either a pyramidal or polarized approach, respectively.\nHowever, most of the current studies examining interval training\nmethods have focused on detecting which of those yields\ngreater improvements on performance, VO2max, and other\nphysiological endurance performance determinants.52 In this\nsense, maybe the correct research question, is rather which is\nthe most effective combination of methods to improve perfor-\nmance and its physiological determinants according to the\nspeciﬁc athlete and competitive goal. Within these different\ncombinations observed, interval training methods typically\nwere conducted at z3 and ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "s marathon, as they accumulate longer distances at,\nor close to, vLT2 pace. Second, this systematic review has\nexamined a very recent article,29 which for the ﬁrst time demon-\nstrated through a 4-armed paralleled control trial that a periodi-\nzation"}
{"chunk_id": "2_elite_periodization_casado_2022_p0012_c0016", "source_registry_id": "src_df9ead131193", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "518f21fecd49554e", "text_span_hash": "518f21fecd49554e", "source_file": "2_elite_periodization_casado_2022.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\2_elite_periodization_casado_2022.pdf", "page": 12, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 16, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "a pyramidal TID. Finally, this is the ﬁrst systematic\nreview on training characteristics in distance runners suggesting\nthat a moderate training volume at z2 speciﬁcally conducted at\nvLT2 or close to this speed is recommended to improve perfor-\nmance", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "The most important consideration derived from the examination\nof the training methods used by highly trained and elite distance\nrunners is that rather than focusing on a single interval training\nmode, the use of several types involving differences in overall\nvolume, number of repetitions and intensity was observed.\nFor example, during a typical training week runners may con-\nduct 2 (or more) different interval training sessions covered at\nvLT2 and vVO2max, respectively.23,29–32,34 More speciﬁcally, at\nleast one continuous or medium/long aerobic interval training\nsession at vLT2/z2, and one anaerobic/short interval training\nsession in z3 per week is required to develop performance\noptimally in highly trained and elite runners.23,27,29,31,34 Elite\nrunners used to increase the number of either vLT2 or z3 sessions\nto adopt either a pyramidal or polarized approach, respectively.\nHowever, most of the current studies examining interval training\nmethods have focused on detecting which of those yields\ngreater improvements on performance, VO2max, and other\nphysiological endurance performance determinants.52 In this\nsense, maybe the correct research question, is rather which is\nthe most effective combination of methods to improve perfor-\nmance and its physiological determinants according to the\nspeciﬁc athlete and competitive goal. Within these different\ncombinations observed, interval training methods typically\nwere conducted at z3 and ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "a pyramidal TID. Finally, this is the ﬁrst systematic\nreview on training characteristics in distance runners suggesting\nthat a moderate training volume at z2 speciﬁcally conducted at\nvLT2 or close to this speed is recommended to improve perfor-\nmance"}
{"chunk_id": "2_elite_periodization_casado_2022_p0012_c0018", "source_registry_id": "src_df9ead131193", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "fdd272fca1a0a2a0", "text_span_hash": "fdd272fca1a0a2a0", "source_file": "2_elite_periodization_casado_2022.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\2_elite_periodization_casado_2022.pdf", "page": 12, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 18, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "on\ntargeted has been found in the literature. Second, 4 of the studies\nreviewed are case studies with limited sample size, which accounts\nfor anecdotical observations rather than generalizations which\ncould lead to general recommendations in training", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "The most important consideration derived from the examination\nof the training methods used by highly trained and elite distance\nrunners is that rather than focusing on a single interval training\nmode, the use of several types involving differences in overall\nvolume, number of repetitions and intensity was observed.\nFor example, during a typical training week runners may con-\nduct 2 (or more) different interval training sessions covered at\nvLT2 and vVO2max, respectively.23,29–32,34 More speciﬁcally, at\nleast one continuous or medium/long aerobic interval training\nsession at vLT2/z2, and one anaerobic/short interval training\nsession in z3 per week is required to develop performance\noptimally in highly trained and elite runners.23,27,29,31,34 Elite\nrunners used to increase the number of either vLT2 or z3 sessions\nto adopt either a pyramidal or polarized approach, respectively.\nHowever, most of the current studies examining interval training\nmethods have focused on detecting which of those yields\ngreater improvements on performance, VO2max, and other\nphysiological endurance performance determinants.52 In this\nsense, maybe the correct research question, is rather which is\nthe most effective combination of methods to improve perfor-\nmance and its physiological determinants according to the\nspeciﬁc athlete and competitive goal. Within these different\ncombinations observed, interval training methods typically\nwere conducted at z3 and ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "on\ntargeted has been found in the literature. Second, 4 of the studies\nreviewed are case studies with limited sample size, which accounts\nfor anecdotical observations rather than generalizations which\ncould lead to general recommendations in training"}
{"chunk_id": "2_elite_periodization_casado_2022_p0012_c0019", "source_registry_id": "src_df9ead131193", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "949871159814e337", "text_span_hash": "949871159814e337", "source_file": "2_elite_periodization_casado_2022.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\2_elite_periodization_casado_2022.pdf", "page": 12, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 19, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "al recommendations in training practice. Third,\nonly 4 experimental studies in this population have been found, the\nrest of the studies reviewed followed an observational approach.\nTherefore, most of the results indicate the outcomes derived from\nthe", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "The most important consideration derived from the examination\nof the training methods used by highly trained and elite distance\nrunners is that rather than focusing on a single interval training\nmode, the use of several types involving differences in overall\nvolume, number of repetitions and intensity was observed.\nFor example, during a typical training week runners may con-\nduct 2 (or more) different interval training sessions covered at\nvLT2 and vVO2max, respectively.23,29–32,34 More speciﬁcally, at\nleast one continuous or medium/long aerobic interval training\nsession at vLT2/z2, and one anaerobic/short interval training\nsession in z3 per week is required to develop performance\noptimally in highly trained and elite runners.23,27,29,31,34 Elite\nrunners used to increase the number of either vLT2 or z3 sessions\nto adopt either a pyramidal or polarized approach, respectively.\nHowever, most of the current studies examining interval training\nmethods have focused on detecting which of those yields\ngreater improvements on performance, VO2max, and other\nphysiological endurance performance determinants.52 In this\nsense, maybe the correct research question, is rather which is\nthe most effective combination of methods to improve perfor-\nmance and its physiological determinants according to the\nspeciﬁc athlete and competitive goal. Within these different\ncombinations observed, interval training methods typically\nwere conducted at z3 and ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "al recommendations in training practice. Third,\nonly 4 experimental studies in this population have been found, the\nrest of the studies reviewed followed an observational approach.\nTherefore, most of the results indicate the outcomes derived from\nthe"}
