a specific running speed. Statistically\nsignificant improvements in RE were observed in\nat least one of the nine studies. Five studies\nassessed RE at a single speed, while four others\nevaluated RE at multiple speeds. Additionally,\nmaximal oxygen uptake and blood lactate\nmeasures to assess other factors influenci", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "ch group, minimal differences\nat baseline were observed for age (38.2 vs. 39.3\nyears), body mass (81.6 vs. 82.2 kg), body height\nmL∙kg⁻¹∙min⁻¹) between the control and HIIT\ngroups. Seven studies included moderately trained\nor recreational runners, on"}
