 a specific running speed. Statistically\nsignificant improvements in RE were observed in\nat least one of the nine studies. Five studies\nassessed RE at a single speed, while four others\nevaluated RE at multiple speeds. Additionally,\nmaximal oxygen uptake and blood lactate\nmeasures to assess other factors influenci", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "onded to speeds below the first ventilatory\nor lactate threshold (approximately 70% VO2max),\nZone 2 (Z2) included speeds between the first and\nVO2max), and Zone 3 (Z3) encompassed speeds\nexceeding the second threshold (above 85%\nVO2max) (Casado et al"}
