er scholars have\nresearchers pointed out that HIIT was particularly\neffective in improving VO2max during the initial\nstages of training for individuals with lower fitness\nimprovements in ventilatory thresholds above the\nsecond ventilatory improvements were only\nobserved in well‐trained endurance runners (Seiler\ne", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "Leite et al., 2023; Nuuttila et al.,\n2022). Additionally, it can lead to decreased\nadherence to training, particularly in unsupervised\nsettings (Ekkekakis and Biddle, 2023; Santos et al.,\n2023). In contrast, MICT is relatively effective in\nmitigating"}
