her scholars have\nresearchers pointed out that HIIT was particularly\neffective in improving VO2max during the initial\nstages of training for individuals with lower fitness\nimprovements in ventilatory thresholds above the\nsecond ventilatory improvements were only\nobserved in well‐trained endurance runners (Seiler\ne", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "olytic capacity, increased oxidative activity,\nand alterations in lactate transport (Denadai et al.,\n2006; Joyner and Coyle, 2008). These benefits\ninclude enhanced recovery of creatine phosphate\nand increased mitochondrial biogenesis, improved\nskelet"}
