l competitive\nprogram with average\n5 years of training for a\nZ2 and 4% in Z3\nperformance and stroke\nrate, distance per stroke,\nspecific swim power and\nswimming performance,\nspecific swim power and\ncompared with TP values", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "González‑Ravé et al. Sports Medicine - Open (2022) 8:56\nTable 3  (continued)\nType of periodization\nTraining characteristics\n7.0 ± 1.5 h of training/\nBody composition, heart\nrate variability, swim‑\nming, maximal horizon‑\ntal jump and running\nperforman"}
