s should be in a structured jump-\nWHAT STRATEGIES CAN BE USED\nFOR YOUTH RUNNERS TO ASSESS\nPSYCHOLOGICAL DEVELOPMENT\nFOR SAFE PARTICIPATION AND\nCreating a safe and supportive envi-\nronment for youth runners may pro-\nmote longevity in the sport, increase\noverall physical activity, and con-\ntribute to psychological well-being.\nYouth runners are developing physi-\ncally and psychologically while", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "ble activity in\nchronic stress that was not mitigated\nby coping efforts (51). Sports special-\nization is more common in today’s\nyouth sport cultures, often deﬁned\nas choosing a single main sport,\ntraining more than 8 months per\nyear, and/or quitting"}
