cceptance, as well as a rigid lever\nfor push-off. Therefore, the foot is natu-\nrally mobile and very well adapted to\nwalk and run without footwear.\nModern shoes have become increasingly\nsupportive, reducing the demand on the\nfoot and reducing foot strength. Evidence\nto support this comes from populations\nthat do not use modern footwear. A\nstudy of 2,300 Indian children revealed\nthat habit", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "and ankle\nstrengthening and softer landings. Youth\nrunners who currently wear traditional\ncushioned shoes and wish to transition\nto minimalist footwear should perform\nadditional strengthening; the process of\nstrengthening the foot and ankle and\nadap"}
