o understand if the type of self-­talk (positive, neutral,\nor negative) and can influence stress-­related parameters, such as perceived exer-\ntion, cardiorespiratory, and cortisol responses. The study's objective was there-\nfore to investigate the top-­down effect of positive and negative self-­talk compared\nto a dissociative activ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "talk, and a dissociative group (DG). First, participants underwent an in-\ncremental running test on a treadmill to determine the maximal oxygen uptake\n(V̇O2max). Next, participants received a mental training session on self-­talk and\ncreated three po"}
