is investigation was to examine\nthe effect of the nature of associative self-­talk and disso-\nciative focus during prolonged running exercise on physi-\nological variables and the perceived exertion. To achieve\nthis goal, we designed the experiment in such a way that\nthe prolonged running exercise-­induced an iso-­metabolic\nstr", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "nd local running clubs to avoid\nthe negative impact of physical inactivity on the metabolic\nΔ rate of perceived exertion (a), minute ventilation (b), breathing frequency (c), and tidal volume (d) as a function of time\nduring the steady-­state running"}
