s, etc.,\nincreases power critical for running.\nCancer survivor, amputee and world champion athlete who ran the NYC Marathon. Danielle is also an All Star on the\nTeam CAF softball team.\n“Running a marathon is all about your mental game. From Day 1, start sharpening it. I mean\nmentally co", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "the\nTeam CAF softball team.\n“Running a marathon is all about your mental game. From Day 1, start sharpening it. I mean\nmentally coaching yourself, preventing yourself from going to dark places during your long\nruns and enjoying the ride. You signed u"}
{"chunk_id": "EWM-Training-Guides-Base-Plan_p0008_c0001", "source_registry_id": "src_d0fd178b5458", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "512f48bda8608b4a", "text_span_hash": "512f48bda8608b4a", "source_file": "EWM-Training-Guides-Base-Plan.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\EWM-Training-Guides-Base-Plan.pdf", "page": 8, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 1, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "Library of video demos\nWarm-ups involve running or movements done at a lower intensity\nand slower pace. They are important because they give your body a\nchance to loosen up, while gradually increasing your heart rate\n(warm up). This improves running", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Library of video demos\nWarm-ups involve running or movements done at a lower intensity\nand slower pace. They are important because they give your body a\nchance to loosen up, while gradually increasing your heart rate\n(warm up). This improves running performance.\nCoaching cue: This is one of the most effective ways to prevent\nA series of stretches that stimulate muscle repair and healing. This\npart of your routine is important because it gives your body a\nchance to loosen up while gradually bringing your heart rate down\nCoaching cue: This time offers you an opportunity to reflect on your\nInstructions: 30 seconds per movement\nWarm-up 1 video demos\nÉ Leg swing side to sid¿\nÉ Leg swing forward/bacË\nInstructions: 30 seconds per movement\nWarm-up 2 video demos\nÉ Alternating hip/hamstrin\u0018\nÉ Runners lunge w/ twis'\nÉ Forward lunge w/ twis'\nInstructions: Hold each for 30 seconds\nCool-down video demos\nÉ Upper-body stretch\nÉ Seated calf stretch\nÉ Downward-facing do\u0018\nÉ Hip and back stretch\nÉ Side-lying quad stretch\nEquipment needed: Variety of dumbbells, a stable chair, a stable step stool or stair tread, a resistance band", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "Library of video demos\nWarm-ups involve running or movements done at a lower intensity\nand slower pace. They are important because they give your body a\nchance to loosen up, while gradually increasing your heart rate\n(warm up). This improves running"}
{"chunk_id": "EWM-Training-Guides-Base-Plan_p0008_c0004", "source_registry_id": "src_d0fd178b5458", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "281496c26fddecdf", "text_span_hash": "281496c26fddecdf", "source_file": "EWM-Training-Guides-Base-Plan.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\EWM-Training-Guides-Base-Plan.pdf", "page": 8, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 4, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "swing side to sid¿\nÉ Leg swing forward/bacË\nInstructions: 30 seconds per movement\nWarm-up 2 video demos\nÉ Alternating hip/hamstrin\u0018\nÉ Runners lunge w/ twis'\nÉ Forward lunge w/ twis'\nInstructions: Hold each for 30 seconds\nCool-down video demos\nÉ Upper", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Library of video demos\nWarm-ups involve running or movements done at a lower intensity\nand slower pace. They are important because they give your body a\nchance to loosen up, while gradually increasing your heart rate\n(warm up). This improves running performance.\nCoaching cue: This is one of the most effective ways to prevent\nA series of stretches that stimulate muscle repair and healing. This\npart of your routine is important because it gives your body a\nchance to loosen up while gradually bringing your heart rate down\nCoaching cue: This time offers you an opportunity to reflect on your\nInstructions: 30 seconds per movement\nWarm-up 1 video demos\nÉ Leg swing side to sid¿\nÉ Leg swing forward/bacË\nInstructions: 30 seconds per movement\nWarm-up 2 video demos\nÉ Alternating hip/hamstrin\u0018\nÉ Runners lunge w/ twis'\nÉ Forward lunge w/ twis'\nInstructions: Hold each for 30 seconds\nCool-down video demos\nÉ Upper-body stretch\nÉ Seated calf stretch\nÉ Downward-facing do\u0018\nÉ Hip and back stretch\nÉ Side-lying quad stretch\nEquipment needed: Variety of dumbbells, a stable chair, a stable step stool or stair tread, a resistance band", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "swing side to sid¿\nÉ Leg swing forward/bacË\nInstructions: 30 seconds per movement\nWarm-up 2 video demos\nÉ Alternating hip/hamstrin\u0018\nÉ Runners lunge w/ twis'\nÉ Forward lunge w/ twis'\nInstructions: Hold each for 30 seconds\nCool-down video demos\nÉ Upper"}
{"chunk_id": "EWM-Training-Guides-Base-Plan_p0009_c0001", "source_registry_id": "src_d0fd178b5458", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "334f4cbdd38193b4", "text_span_hash": "334f4cbdd38193b4", "source_file": "EWM-Training-Guides-Base-Plan.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\EWM-Training-Guides-Base-Plan.pdf", "page": 9, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 1, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "Library of video demos\nStrength work prevents injuries by strengthening muscles and connective tissues. This program includes two strength-training blocks. Block 1 includes\na weekly total body anterior workout and then posterior workouts in weeks 1-5", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Library of video demos\nStrength work prevents injuries by strengthening muscles and connective tissues. This program includes two strength-training blocks. Block 1 includes\na weekly total body anterior workout and then posterior workouts in weeks 1-5. Then, in weeks 6-12 you’ll follow Block 2. Block 2 also has weekly total\nbody anterior and posterior workouts, but it advances all of the exercises from Block 1 to challenge your body and allow your musculoskeletal system\nto get stronger. This is called progressive overload, and it allows for a gradual adaptation while minimizing the risk of injury.\nEquipment needed: Variety of dumbbells, a stable chair, a stable step stool or stair tread, a resistance band\nLibrary of video demos\nMobility Instructions: 2x 8 rep\n Forward hip circle\n Backward hip circles\nLibrary of video demos\nAnkle/Foot Instructions: 2x 8 rep\n Ankle dorsiflexioÉ\n Ankle plantar flexioÉ\n Single-leg balance\nLibrary of video demos\nInstructions: 3x 10-12 rep\n Standing knee drives + Wt\nLibrary of video demos\nTotal Body Posterior\nInstructions: 3x 10-12 rep\n Supine knee drives", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "Library of video demos\nStrength work prevents injuries by strengthening muscles and connective tissues. This program includes two strength-training blocks. Block 1 includes\na weekly total body anterior workout and then posterior workouts in weeks 1-5"}
