e reduction in physical activity can result in over-\nall physical deconditioning and can increase the risk of cardiovascular problems in time\nAchilles tendinopathy causes pain, swelling, and thickening in the AT, and ulti-\nmately impairs health-promoting activities [17]. It most often occurs in the mid-substance\nof the tendon (55–65%) and l", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "o be an effective method for assessing the risk of high Achilles tendinopathy\nbased on the correlation between the CSA and height, sex, height, miles run per week, and\nConsidering that there are modifiable (e.g., running distance, duration) and unmod"}
