e reduction in physical activity can result in over-\nall physical deconditioning and can increase the risk of cardiovascular problems in time\nAchilles tendinopathy causes pain, swelling, and thickening in the AT, and ulti-\nmately impairs health-promoting activities [17]. It most often occurs in the mid-substance\nof the tendon (55–65%) and l", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "for patients with chronic Achilles tendi-\nnosis. Another study supports that this training method may improve clinical results for\nthese patients [24]. However, more recently, both isometric and functional strengthening\nhave been promoted. The purpo"}
