ogether,\nthey allow the femur to act in all 3\ntransverse—performing\nsion, ﬂexion, abduction, adduction,\ninternal rotation, and external rota-\nRunning is primarily a sagittal plane\nactivity, with hip extension serving\nas a fundamental movement pattern.\nHip extension is largely responsible\nforces necessary to move the body\n", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "most powerful, and\nmuscles. (22) Therefore, it is not sur-\nprising that runners and athletic pro-\nstrengthening the gluteus maximus\nas a way to improve force production,\nrunning speed, and performance. It is\nnotable that common strength exer-\nlunges,"}
