velocity (negative pacing) throughout\nmarathon (16) and 10-k races (15) more\nthan women, coaches and male runners\nshould make concerted efforts to address\nthis trend. Older and likely more experi-\nenced runners exhibit less slowing over\na race (15,16) consistent with the thought\nthat pacing is a skill to be practiced and\ncrafted over years of experience (19).\nThere is not a single “optimal", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "nces\nbetween experienced and novice time trial\ncyclists. Med Sci Sports Exerc 49: 1884–\nBrick NE, Campbell MJ, Metcalfe RS, Mair\nJL, and Macintyre TE. Altering pace control\nand pace regulation: Attentional focus\neffects during running. Med Sci Sports"}
