elocity (negative pacing) throughout\nmarathon (16) and 10-k races (15) more\nthan women, coaches and male runners\nshould make concerted efforts to address\nthis trend. Older and likely more experi-\nenced runners exhibit less slowing over\na race (15,16) consistent with the thought\nthat pacing is a skill to be practiced and\ncrafted over years of experience (19).\nThere is not a single “optimal", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "roads lead to Rome?\nFront Physiol 5: 73, 2014.\nCheuvront SN and Montain SJ. Myths and\nmethodologies: Making sense of exercise\nPacing Strategy in Running\nVOLUME 42 | NUMBER 1 | FEBRUARY 2020\nCopyright © National Strength and Conditioning Association."}
