lanned recovery. Consider the possibilities in skill instruction, acquisition and the\nproposed goals throughout the phases as principal drivers of the training process will permit an optimal and\nflexible determination of the most appropriate training methods and ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "d Human Performance: Lippincott Williams & Wilkins. 2013.\n10. HELLSTEN-WESTING Y, NORMAN B, BALSOM PD, SJODIN B. Decreased resting levels of\nadenine nucleotides in human skeletal muscle after high-intensity training. J Appl Physiol. 1993;\n11. HOFF J."}
