ting, etc. Thus, the example rowing\ntraining session above may be further described as three repetitions of ten minutes of\nwork at a rating of 26 strokes per minute while maintaining a heart rate of 140 to 170.\nIn a systematic plan of training, the training load goes from quantity to quality. This\nmeans that, after a period of adjustin", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "is enables the development of the specific needs\nof the sport of rowing and the necessary performance capabilities to achieve the training\nAlthough this procedure is for the major part of the programme, it must be considered\nas a guide because traini"}
