re widely accepted.\nSpeciﬁcally, gait retraining seems to\nbe a viable strategy for runners deal-\ning with RRI including patellofe-\nmoral pain (PFP) syndrome (94)\nmodes vary from simple (e.g., step\nrate manipulation) to complex (e.g.,\nwith strategies that can be clinic- or\nﬁeld-based (93). Numerous publica-\ntions have critically reviewed these\nseems to be mounting cli", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "erm adoption of running\ngait changes are limited; however,\nsome evidence suggest that changes\ncan persist for 1 month (21,66) to 3\nmonths (94). With recognition that\na runner can actively change their\ngait for RRI reasons, the question nat-\nurally be"}
