e widely accepted.\nSpeciﬁcally, gait retraining seems to\nbe a viable strategy for runners deal-\ning with RRI including patellofe-\nmoral pain (PFP) syndrome (94)\nmodes vary from simple (e.g., step\nrate manipulation) to complex (e.g.,\nwith strategies that can be clinic- or\nﬁeld-based (93). Numerous publica-\ntions have critically reviewed these\nseems to be mounting cli", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "s, the question nat-\nurally becomes “Can a runner actively\nchange their running gait for perfor-\nmance improvements?”\nRunning performance is primarily\ndetermined by the combined inﬂu-\nence of maximal aerobic capacity\n(9), lactate threshold (82), and"}
