ore widely accepted.\nSpeciﬁcally, gait retraining seems to\nbe a viable strategy for runners deal-\ning with RRI including patellofe-\nmoral pain (PFP) syndrome (94)\nmodes vary from simple (e.g., step\nrate manipulation) to complex (e.g.,\nwith strategies that can be clinic- or\nﬁeld-based (93). Numerous publica-\ntions have critically reviewed these\nseems to be mounting cli", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": ", lactate threshold (82), and run-\nning economy (RE) (17). To some\nextent, all 3 factors can be improved\nwith appropriate training methods;\nhowever, RE can vary substantially\nbetween runners of similar aerobic\ncapacities indicating that it is a key\nc"}
