lish the goal. Conversely,\na local feedback strategy targets a spe-\nciﬁc gait feature and explicitly attempts\nto adjust it. For instance, runners with\nPFP have been provided visual feedback\non knee position with instructions to\nlimit its valgus movement during the\nAlthough generally accepted ﬂaws such\nas extraneous upper-extremity motion\nare thought to lead to poor ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "posed to a “one size ﬁts\nall” approach. Although we are not stat-\ning that gait retraining cannot assist an\nindividual runner to become more eco-\nnomical, clear knowledge of what bio-\nmechanical criteria to correct across\nmany or all runners is lacki"}
