plish the goal. Conversely,\na local feedback strategy targets a spe-\nciﬁc gait feature and explicitly attempts\nto adjust it. For instance, runners with\nPFP have been provided visual feedback\non knee position with instructions to\nlimit its valgus movement during the\nAlthough generally accepted ﬂaws such\nas extraneous upper-extremity motion\nare thought to lead to poor ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "s\nmany or all runners is lacking. Despite\nthis uncertainty, we will discuss clini-\ncally feasible interventions for individu-\nmanipulation. With the advent of wear-\nable technology to measure and track\n(VOSC), and high-speed video becom-\ning standard"}
