ssed RE. Evidence\nsuggest that both experienced and inex-\nperienced runners may self-optimize to\nthe most economical pairing of stride\nlength and stride rate (14,47). In addition,\nrunners demonstrate the ability to main-\ntain the self-optimization of spatiotem-\nporal mechanics even when fatigued\n(87). To date, a one size ﬁts all “optimal”\nstride rate/length for impr", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "ing\nstride length. Runners received 15 mi-\nnutes of visual-audio feedback over 15\nsessions in a 3-week period to retrain\ntheir gait timing in accordance with\nan increased stride rate. After retraining,\nlength and RE signiﬁcantly improved\nby 3.4%. Ove"}
