sed RE. Evidence\nsuggest that both experienced and inex-\nperienced runners may self-optimize to\nthe most economical pairing of stride\nlength and stride rate (14,47). In addition,\nrunners demonstrate the ability to main-\ntain the self-optimization of spatiotem-\nporal mechanics even when fatigued\n(87). To date, a one size ﬁts all “optimal”\nstride rate/length for impr", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "of a NRFS\npoint to the high incidence of elite\nendurance runners using an NRFS\n(72); however, this has been ques-\ntioned by surveys of foot strike patterns\nduring races (39,40). The foot strike\npattern adopted by runners may be\nspeed dependent, with"}
