g the role of adductor strength and length as\npants physiological differences and training surfaces\nwell as age and/or sport experience as risk factors\ncan all lead to differences between the injured and\nnon-injured groups in all the reviewed studies. Inter-\nventional studies did not report how poten", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "ry. Non randomisation in\ngreater abductor to adductor strength ratios as well\nthe intervention studies, and non-matching in the\nas sport specificity of training and pre-season sport-\nquasiexperimental studies contributes to an inability\nspecific trai"}
