. Again, they had the option to answer ‘I don’t talk to myself’. In total, there were 20\nquestions about self-talk specifics. A machine learning model was not suitable to predict the difference between high and low intensity\nquestions as the high intensity/low intensity paired structure of the items would be lost. Instead, we tested this difference with", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "t, or\nconcerning other people) under high-pressure and low-pressure conditions. They could also answer ‘I don’t talk to myself’. High-\npressure questions were initiated with the sentence fragment ‘When I push myself while running…’ and Low-pressure q"}
