reased during the middle and late\nstages of the race. For optimal 24 h ultra-marathon\nperformance, the “big three” strategies of training,\nnutrition, and pacing are all important.\n34 experienced endurance runners in the\nStour Valley Path 100kmUltramarathon\nDeviations in average speed from\nA positive pacing pattern was observed in the ultra-\nmarathon.Pe", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "the half-marathon. Most age groups in both genders exhibited a more\neven pace in the half-marathon than in the marathon.\n279 finishers in Berlin’s Marathon from\nAverage speed from each\nPositive pacing behaviors were predominantly followed by elite ma"}
