arily in the magnitude of speed change,\nwith no significant differences in overall profiles. Only two studies reported inconsistent pacing strategies between the genders, with\none indicating that men used negative pacing and women did not; the other noted that males decreased their pacing at 25–30 km,\nRegarding age, ten studies yielded tw", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "hon but not during the half marathon. For the pacing strategy, the full and half marathons were similar\nto the positive pacing strategy, but sometimes negative pacing was observed in the half marathon [17,26–29].\nThere are also some studies on the pa"}
