trategy. Robert et al.\nobserved that male athletes experience a more significant speed reduction during races compared to female athletes, likely due to\nhigher initial energy expenditure [69,74]. Both psychological motives, such as competitive early pacing [69], and physiological as-\npects, such as nerve fatigue and muscle glycogen deplet", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "ormalized speed comparisons between all\nathletes as well as between the marathon and half-marathon.\nDif-half:Difference in relative speed between the first half of the marathon and the second half.\nEnd Spurt(ES):running speed for the last segment was"}
