stribution but also significantly influences training costs.\nSwain et al. analyzed training across various marathon events and found no substantial differences in training duration or race\nexperience among athletes, though pacing strategies varied [16]. The requirements for shorter events demand more intensive training\nrelative to longer", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "e pacing strategy\nMarathons, categorized into half-marathons (21.0975 km), full marathons (42.195 km), and ultramarathons (exceeding 42.195\nkm), demonstrate varied pacing strategies across distances, with consensus in the literature on this variabili"}
