orted by the involvement of a second author to validate the results of the scale, as the interrater reliability of\nthe NOS has been critically examined [86]. However, the sensitivity of the NOS might be questioned. For example, the first question of\nthe scale concerning the representativeness of the exposed cohort, and both options (a) ‘t", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "r extended periods and distances [85].\nTraining should also be aligned with runners to comprehend the volume and intensity of training. This finding aligns with their\nperformance pacing in races to enhance the understanding of their pacing strategies"}
