. Sports Exerc. 2003, 35, 488–494. [CrossRef]\nSchneider, D.A.; Lacroix, K.A.; Atkinson, G.R.; Troped, P.J.; Pollack, J. Ventilatory Threshold and Maximal Oxygen Uptake during\nCycling and Running in Triathletes. Med. Sci. Sports Exerc. 1990, 22, 257–264. [CrossRef] [PubMed]\nBeattie, K.; Kenny, I.C.; Lyons, M.; Carson, B.P. The Effect of Strength Training on Perfo", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "rformance and Running Economy in Well-Trained Athletes. Eur. J. Appl. Physiol. 2006, 97, 1.\nSaunders, P.U.; Pyne, D.B.; Telford, R.D.; Hawley, J.A. Factors Affecting Running Economy in Trained Distance Runners. Sports\nLi, F.; Wang, R.; Newton, R.U.;"}
{"chunk_id": "Resistance_Exercise_Running_Economy_Injury_Narrative_2022_p0011_c0013", "source_registry_id": "src_6922229c7b09", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "c3b19e1e6d8bed04", "text_span_hash": "c3b19e1e6d8bed04", "source_file": "Resistance_Exercise_Running_Economy_Injury_Narrative_2022.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\Resistance_Exercise_Running_Economy_Injury_Narrative_2022.pdf", "page": 11, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 13, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": ", F.; Wang, R.; Newton, R.U.; Sutton, D.; Shi, Y.; Ding, H. Effects of Complex Training versus Heavy Resistance Training on\nNeuromuscular Adaptation, Running Economy and 5-Km Performance in Well-Trained Distance Runners. PeerJ 2019, 7, e6787.\nSasaki,", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "ning; however, biofeedback training is probably more effective for altering overall running\nbiomechanics. RE may help reduce running-related injury risk, although the evidence is\nscarce. In this regard, we recommend that all major lower limb muscle groups be targeted\nif no speciﬁc deﬁcits are present.\nAuthor Contributions: Conceptualization, A.Š., P.Š., J.P. and Ž.K.; methodology, A.Š., P.Š., J.P. and\nŽ.K.; investigation, A.Š., P.Š. and J.P.; data curation, A.Š., P.Š., J.P. and Ž.K.; writing—original draft\npreparation, A.Š., P.Š. and J.P.; writing—review and editing, Ž.K.; visualization, A.Š., P.Š., J.P. and\nŽ.K.; supervision, Ž.K. All authors have read and agreed to the published version of the manuscript.\nInstitutional Review Board Statement: Not applicable.\nInformed Consent Statement: Not applicable.\nData Availability Statement: Not applicable.\nConﬂicts of Interest: The authors declare no conﬂict of interest.\nNevill, A.M.; Brown, D.; Godfrey, R.; Johnson, P.J.; Romer, L.; Stewart, A.D.; Winter, E.M. Modeling Maximum Oxygen Uptake of\nElite Endurance Athletes. Med. Sc