s when dealing with low-risk BSI locations, due\nto the lack of consistency between clinical and radiological\nhealing and the limited sensitivity of radiographs [5, 27, 33,\n34, 68, 70, 72, 82, 84, 89]. In the case of a high-risk BSI,\nsuch as anterior tibial cortex BSI, 23% of studies specified\nimag", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "this walking distance three times [72,\n85]; however, the number of repetitions was not specified in\nForty percent of reviewed studies stated that bony ten-\nderness should have resolved before introducing running-\nstudies, which were either clinical"}
