und reaction force during squat jump.\nStrength and Conditioning Journal | www.nsca-scj.com\nCopyright © National Strength and Conditioning Association. Unauthorized reproduction of this article is prohibited.", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "Summary of studies (n 5 3) that have investigated the effects of a strength training (ST) intervention on adolescent endurance runners\nParticipants, n (I/C),\nMain strength outcomes\nMain running-related\njumps, A-skips, hurdle\nRT (2–3 3 6–8 reps): back"}
