’: the ‘niggle’, the ‘persisting niggle’, and the ‘non-responding niggle’. These\nthree entities describe levels of injury which become increasingly more severe in terms of their\nphysical description, their outcome (effect on running and daily life), their psychological\ndescrip", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "tance of non-time loss injuries, and does so through monitoring both the character-\nistics of pain (physical descriptor) and effect on running (outcome) [15]. However, our find-\nings build upon the OSTRC-O, indicating the importance of capturing addi"}
