njury development, and ensure\npatients understand that it is normal to experience these responses (i.e. to experience anxiety\nor concern, especially with a lower level injury) [55]. Similarly, in helping athletes manage inju-\nries, coaches need to be aware of the importance of n", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "ive of the global\npopulation of runners. In particular, specific terminology used (e.g. niggle) or methods of\nmanagement employed (e.g., access to clinicians) may not be consistent across other nationali-\nties or socio-demographics. Furthermore, as w"}
