that are supported\nby the literature. Progressive resistance\ntraining is a tried and true method of\nincreasing maximal strength, rate of\nforce development, and muscular power\n(3,36). Each of these qualities are bene-\nﬁcial for the distance runner; however,\nmany running athletes have not imple-\nmented concurrent training into their\nprogramming due to a lack of knowledge\nor misconceptions. Con", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "Florida\nA B S T R A C T\nConcurrent training, deﬁned as resis-\ntance training sessions programmed\nalongside endurance training sessions\nduring the same cycle, is a tool that\nhighly trained runners can use to\naugment performance. A review of the\ncurren"}
