g to cover a given\ndistance (5). Jung describes that a run-\nner requiring a lower V̇O2 at the given\nvelocity has better economy. Improved\nrunning economy allows a runner to\nrun faster over a given distance or to\nrun longer at a constant speed due to\nreduced consumption of oxygen (21).\nIn a recent systematic review including\nperforming concurrent high-load resis-\nmaximum [RM] or isometric 6", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "and\ndescribed below in this review.\nAccording to a review by Blagrove\net al., (10) the training variables that\nhave the greatest impact on RunE\ninclude the prescription of multi-joint\nfree-weight exercises as compared to\nmachine and single-joint exer"}
