just stood there looking\ndown at their legs. Some just sat down and crawled away.\nOne or two tried to walk, but without success. Clearly,\nthe newly walking infant was perturbed by the weight.\nTwo weeks later, all the infants were willing to attempt a\nstep or two with the weights. But it was not until 1\nmonth of walking experience that the infan", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "lking without a weight.\nNo differences were found in temporal phasing variabil-\nity, suggesting that the weight did not make the\ninterlimb coordination less stable.\nThus, after 1 month of walking experience, our\nyoung novice walkers had found an attr"}
