just stood there looking\ndown at their legs. Some just sat down and crawled away.\nOne or two tried to walk, but without success. Clearly,\nthe newly walking infant was perturbed by the weight.\nTwo weeks later, all the infants were willing to attempt a\nstep or two with the weights. But it was not until 1\nmonth of walking experience that the infan", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "g legs act as\ncoupled limit-cycle systems, we began by mapping the\naction of the segments in state space. As described\nearlier, the state space is a geometric space within\nwhich our dynamical system (i.e., the walking leg) can\nbe described. Figure 1"}
