 just stood there looking\ndown at their legs. Some just sat down and crawled away.\nOne or two tried to walk, but without success. Clearly,\nthe newly walking infant was perturbed by the weight.\nTwo weeks later, all the infants were willing to attempt a\nstep or two with the weights. But it was not until 1\nmonth of walking experience that the infan", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "g) can\nbe described. Figure 1 is a state space description of\nthe shank's action during four cycles of walking as de-\nfined by the state variables of angular position and\nvelocity of the segment (for a description of the thigh,\nsee Clark, Truly, 8c P"}
