 but one that is\nAlthough the behavior of a single segment, such as\nthe shank or the thigh, is revealing, it does not directly\naddress coordination within the leg. To examine the\nintralimb coordination, we need a measure of the rela-\ntionship between the shank's trajectory in state space and\nthe thigh's trajectory (or the foot). To calculate t", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "the adult. In the adult\nwalker, the phasing relationship from toe-off (0% of the\nwalking cycle) to heelstrike (-40% of the walking cycle)\nbegins at about -80°, with the thigh moving through\nstate space ahead of the shank. (Note that in our mea-\nsure"}
