{"chunk_id": "Stoggl_2014_Polarized_vs_Threshold_p0006_c0007", "source_registry_id": "src_d4dd1dca785a", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "6181c0d8614b6851", "text_span_hash": "6181c0d8614b6851", "source_file": "Stoggl_2014_Polarized_vs_Threshold.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\Stoggl_2014_Polarized_vs_Threshold.pdf", "page": 6, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 7, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "improved after POL\n(−4.8 ± 7.6%, P < 0.05) with no signiﬁcant differences between\nthe other training groups.\nThe changes in TTE, V/Ppeak and V/P2 & 4 from pre- to post-\ntraining and between the single training groups are presented in\nTable 3. The lar", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Endurance training concepts\nThe values presented are means ± SD. F and P values were obtained by Two-Way ANOVA (2 × 4: time × training group) with repeated measures. POL, polarized training group; HIIT, High intensity interval training\ngroup; THR, threshold training group; HVT, high volume training group; VO2, oxygen uptake; HR, heart rate; LApeak, peak blood lactate concentration; *p < 0.05; **p < 0.01; ***p < 0.001 signiﬁcant difference\nwithin groups from pre- to post-training. †p < 0.05; †††p < 0.001 signiﬁcant different from POL training group.‡p < 0.05 signiﬁcant different from HIIT training group. aMain effect between pre- and post-test.\nbMain effect between training groups. ctime × training group interactive effect.\n0.05). The change in VO2peak in POL was higher compared to\nincreased in POL by 10.4 ± 7.9% (P < 0.001), which was greater\ncompared with the other training concepts (HIIT and HVT P <\n0.05, THR P < 0.001). No changes from pre to post and no dif-\nferences between training groups with respect to HRpeak, LApeak,\nand HR2 & 4 were detected (P > 0.05). Work economy increased\nfollowing HIIT (−6.7 ± 4.4% decrease in HR, P < 0.01) and\nTHR (−2.7 ± 1.0% decrease in HR, P < 0.05) with no signif-\nicant differences between the other concepts. Work economy\nexpressed as percent of VO2peak was only improved after POL\n(−4.8 ± 7.6%, P < 0.05) with no signiﬁcant differences between\nthe other training groups.\nThe changes in TTE, V", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "improved after POL\n(−4.8 ± 7.6%, P < 0.05) with no signiﬁcant differences between\nthe other training groups.\nThe changes in TTE, V/Ppeak and V/P2 & 4 from pre- to post-\ntraining and between the single training groups are presented in\nTable 3. The lar"}
