l\nabove (∼15–20%) the LT, but little at the LT. In the current study,\nPOL mimicked this distribution (LOW = 68%, LTP = 6%, HIGH\n= 26%). Only the study of Neal et al. (2013) demonstrated that\n6 weeks of POL resulted in greater systemic adaptation in trained\ncyclists when compared to THR, hen", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "by One-Way ANOVA (4 training groups) calculated over the per cent differences between pre-\nto post-training. POL, polarized training group; HIIT, High intensity interval training group; THR, threshold training group; HVT, high volume training group;"}
