ell\nabove (∼15–20%) the LT, but little at the LT. In the current study,\nPOL mimicked this distribution (LOW = 68%, LTP = 6%, HIGH\n= 26%). Only the study of Neal et al. (2013) demonstrated that\n6 weeks of POL resulted in greater systemic adaptation in trained\ncyclists when compared to THR, hen", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "T, high volume training group; TTE, time\nto exhaustion during the ramp test; V/P2, velocity or power at 2 mmol·L−1; V/P4, velocity or power at 4 mmol·L−1; V/Ppeak, peak velocity or power in the incremental\ntest; *p < 0.05; **p < 0.01; ***p < 0.001 si"}
