r perceptual and\nreactive neurocognitive challenges.6 7 This\nframework moves from high control to\nhigh chaos, and is based on more than a\ndecade of rehabilitation and RTS in the\ndemanding setting of English Premier\nThe control-chaos continuum\nUsing retrospective player chronic running\nloads (GPS) ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "us that incor-\nporates technical aspects, moving from\ncontrol to increasing levels of chaos.\nThe week is structured to overload game\ncomponents using ‘intensive’ and ‘exten-\nsive’ football to increase training speci-\nficity.9 Intensive football overl"}
{"chunk_id": "Taberner_2019_Return_to_Sport_p0002_c0004", "source_registry_id": "src_187b42bfde9e", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "e856189d69bb2910", "text_span_hash": "e856189d69bb2910", "source_file": "Taberner_2019_Return_to_Sport.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\Taberner_2019_Return_to_Sport.pdf", "page": 2, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 4, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "erity. ACC, accelerations; BW, bodyweight; COD, change of direction; DEC, decelerations; Exp-D, explosive distance (accelerating/decelerating from 2 to 4 ms−1 <1 s); HSR, high-speed running (>5.5 ms−1);\nMS, maximal speed; MAXHR, maximal heart rate; P", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Taberner M, et al. Br J Sports Med Month 2019 Vol 0 No 0\nFigure 1  Return to sport framework - the control-chaos continuum. Control=high level of structure on behaviour/actions/movement, that is, controlled situation. Chaos=unpredictable behaviour/actions/\nmovement, as to appear random/reactive, that is, chaotic situation. Green represents high control (low intensity) moving towards high chaos (high intensity). Model can be adjusted according to specific\ninjury diagnosis, estimated tissue healing times and expected return to training. Acc/Dec Magnitude =rate of change in velocity, for example, 3 ms−2.**Game load adjustable dependent on injury type/\nseverity. ACC, accelerations; BW, bodyweight; COD, change of direction; DEC, decelerations; Exp-D, explosive distance (accelerating/decelerating from 2 to 4 ms−1 <1 s); HSR, high-speed running (>5.5 ms−1);\nMS, maximal speed; MAXHR, maximal heart rate; PR, passive recovery; SPR, sprint distance (>7 ms−1); TD, total distance.\non 8 February 2019 by guest. Protected by copyright.\nhttp://bjsm.bmj.com/\nBr J Sports Med: first published as 10.1136/bjsports-2018-100157 on 8 February 2019. Downloaded from", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "erity. ACC, accelerations; BW, bodyweight; COD, change of direction; DEC, decelerations; Exp-D, explosive distance (accelerating/decelerating from 2 to 4 ms−1 <1 s); HSR, high-speed running (>5.5 ms−1);\nMS, maximal speed; MAXHR, maximal heart rate; P"}
