er diagnostics for phase progression during return to sport (RTS)\nConsiderations for RTS load planning\nStrength/power diagnostics\nProgression of running speeds (>70% maximal speed)\nProgression of acceleration/deceleration magnitudes (intensity)\nAppropriate stage to combine sprint distance and ch", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "sprint distance)\nProgression of running speeds (>70% maximal speed)\nProgression of acceleration/deceleration frequency and magnitudes (explosive distance)\nIso soleus/gastrocnemius PF, RFD (FP)\nSL/DL CMJ jump height, force/power/impulse and asymmetrie"}
{"chunk_id": "Taberner_2019_Return_to_Sport_p0004_c0012", "source_registry_id": "src_187b42bfde9e", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "cb35cbc88686bd3c", "text_span_hash": "cb35cbc88686bd3c", "source_file": "Taberner_2019_Return_to_Sport.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\Taberner_2019_Return_to_Sport.pdf", "page": 4, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 12, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "Progression of technical actions—passing, crossing, shooting, tackling\nAppropriate stage to combine change of direction, at speed, under chaotic conditions\nIso hip abductor/adductor; PF (GroinBar)\nProgression of running volumes (total distance, HSR,", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Taberner M, et al. Br J Sports Med Month 2019 Vol 0 No 0\nfrom short/mid/long range while jumping/\nheading and tackling; graded in inten-\nsity as static/movement/in-context. The\nvolume of technical actions should be\nprogressively increased and be player and\nIn the final phase, we emphasise posi-\ntion-specific conditioning and reflect\ngame intensity with volumes relative\nto weekly preinjury training outputs.\ndurance drills (online supplementary\nvideos 9 and 10) prepare players for\ngame activity—where the speed/direc-\ntion of the pass dictates how fast the\nplayer moves. Technical considerations\nspecific to the injury in question (eg,\nball striking activity for a groin injury)\nform part of our final criteria for return\nto training, alongside strength and\npower diagnostics (table 1).\nIn an elite environment, RTS is a dynamic\nprocess balancing the benefits and risks of\nRTS to the player and the team.2 The CCC\nmoves from high control to high chaos,\nprescribing running loads under progres-\nsively riskier conditions. The continuum is\nthe product of scientific evidence blended\nTable 1  Injury-specific load planning considerations and strength/power diagnostics for phase progression during return to sport (RTS)\nConsiderations for RTS load planning\nStrength/power diagnostics\nProgression of running speeds (>70% maximal speed)\nProgression of acceleration/deceleration magnitudes (intensity)\nAppropriate stage to combine sprint distance and ch", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "Progression of technical actions—passing, crossing, shooting, tackling\nAppropriate stage to combine change of direction, at speed, under chaotic conditions\nIso hip abductor/adductor; PF (GroinBar)\nProgression of running volumes (total distance, HSR,"}
