ower diagnostics for phase progression during return to sport (RTS)\nConsiderations for RTS load planning\nStrength/power diagnostics\nProgression of running speeds (>70% maximal speed)\nProgression of acceleration/deceleration magnitudes (intensity)\nAppropriate stage to combine sprint distance and ch", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "SL drop jump RSI (FP)\nIso squat/mid-thigh pull PF, RFD (FP)\nIso soleus/gastrocnemius PF, RFD (FP)\nIso posterior chain PF, RFD, SE (FP)\nEcc hamstring PF (NHE)\nIso hip abductor/adductor PF (GroinBar)\nspecific, ie, stress\nProgression of running volumes"}
