s. The most common initial symp-\ntom of frostbite is numbness. During\nrewarming, pain is signiﬁcant, and re-\nwarming should be clinically super-\nvised for all but the most minor injuries.\nFROSTBITE PREVENTION\nThe Wind Chill Temperature Index\n(WCTI, Figure 2) is the best indicator\nof frostbite risk. It takes into account\nthe air temperature, and wind speed\nand estimates the rate at which t", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "of exposed facial skin (12). How-\never, the WCTI was developed for in-\ndividuals who are not exercising, so, in\nrunners who are exercising at high\nintensities, it will overestimate the risk\nof frostbite. One important point is that\nrunners will creat"}
