es. The most common initial symp-\ntom of frostbite is numbness. During\nrewarming, pain is signiﬁcant, and re-\nwarming should be clinically super-\nvised for all but the most minor injuries.\nFROSTBITE PREVENTION\nThe Wind Chill Temperature Index\n(WCTI, Figure 2) is the best indicator\nof frostbite risk. It takes into account\nthe air temperature, and wind speed\nand estimates the rate at which t", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "int is that\nrunners will create their own wind;\ntherefore, the speed that individuals\nare running at needs to be accounted\nfor when estimating the WCTI. Gen-\nerally, the risk of frostbite is less than\n5% when the ambient temperature is\nabove 2158C, b"}
