wangen, Germany\nObjective: Finishing a marathon requires to prepare for a 42.2 km run. Current literature\ndescribes which training characteristics are related to marathon performance. However,\nwhich training is most effective in terms of a performance improvement remains unclear.\nMethods: W", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "(2021) Retrospective\nAnalysis of Training and Its Response\nin Marathon Finishers Based on\nRetrospective Analysis of Training\nand Its Response in Marathon\nFinishers Based on Fitness App Data\nMarkus Zrenner 1*, Christian Heyde 2, Burkhard Duemler 3, S"}
{"chunk_id": "train_app_data_marathon_2021_p0001_c0007", "source_registry_id": "src_cc72f1165e30", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "dc4fdf0b69e93030", "text_span_hash": "dc4fdf0b69e93030", "source_file": "train_app_data_marathon_2021.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\train_app_data_marathon_2021.pdf", "page": 1, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 7, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "marathon performance. However,\nwhich training is most effective in terms of a performance improvement remains unclear.\nMethods: We conducted a retrospective analysis of training responses during a 16\nweeks training period prior to an absolved marath", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Frontiers in Physiology | www.frontiersin.org\nMay 2021 | Volume 12 | Article 669884\nPantelis Theodoros Nikolaidis,\nUniversity of West Attica, Greece\nSingidunum University, Serbia\nUniversity College Dublin, Ireland\nNortheastern University, United States\nmarkus.zrenner@fau.de\nThis article was submitted to\nExercise Physiology,\na section of the journal\nFrontiers in Physiology\nZrenner M, Heyde C, Duemler B,\nDykman S, Roecker K and\nEskoﬁer BM (2021) Retrospective\nAnalysis of Training and Its Response\nin Marathon Finishers Based on\nRetrospective Analysis of Training\nand Its Response in Marathon\nFinishers Based on Fitness App Data\nMarkus Zrenner 1*, Christian Heyde 2, Burkhard Duemler 3, Solms Dykman 4, Kai Roecker 5\nand Bjoern M. Eskoﬁer 1\n1 Machine Learning and Data Analytics Lab, Department Artiﬁcial Intelligence in Biomedical Engineering, University of\nErlangen-Nürnberg (FAU), Erlangen, Germany, 2 Adidas AG, Future Sport Science, Herzogenaurach, Germany, 3 Adidas AG,\nTechnology & Innovation, Herzogenaurach, Germany, 4 Runtastic GmbH, Pasching, Austria, 5 Institute for Applied Public\nHealth and Exercise Medicine, Furtwangen University (HFU), Furtwangen, Germany\nObjective: Finishing a marathon requires to prepare for a 42.2 km run. Current literature\ndescribes which training characteristics are related to marathon performance. However,\nwhich training is most effective in terms of a performance improvement remains unclear.\nMethods: W", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "marathon performance. However,\nwhich training is most effective in terms of a performance improvement remains unclear.\nMethods: We conducted a retrospective analysis of training responses during a 16\nweeks training period prior to an absolved marath"}
{"chunk_id": "train_app_data_marathon_2021_p0001_c0008", "source_registry_id": "src_cc72f1165e30", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "b41c8727d0a9b8f3", "text_span_hash": "b41c8727d0a9b8f3", "source_file": "train_app_data_marathon_2021.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\train_app_data_marathon_2021.pdf", "page": 1, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 8, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "od prior to an absolved marathon. The analysis was performed on\nunsupervised ﬁtness app data (Runtastic) from 6,771 marathon ﬁnishers. Differences in\ntraining volume and intensity between three response and three marathon performance\ngroups were anal", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Frontiers in Physiology | www.frontiersin.org\nMay 2021 | Volume 12 | Article 669884\nPantelis Theodoros Nikolaidis,\nUniversity of West Attica, Greece\nSingidunum University, Serbia\nUniversity College Dublin, Ireland\nNortheastern University, United States\nmarkus.zrenner@fau.de\nThis article was submitted to\nExercise Physiology,\na section of the journal\nFrontiers in Physiology\nZrenner M, Heyde C, Duemler B,\nDykman S, Roecker K and\nEskoﬁer BM (2021) Retrospective\nAnalysis of Training and Its Response\nin Marathon Finishers Based on\nRetrospective Analysis of Training\nand Its Response in Marathon\nFinishers Based on Fitness App Data\nMarkus Zrenner 1*, Christian Heyde 2, Burkhard Duemler 3, Solms Dykman 4, Kai Roecker 5\nand Bjoern M. Eskoﬁer 1\n1 Machine Learning and Data Analytics Lab, Department Artiﬁcial Intelligence in Biomedical Engineering, University of\nErlangen-Nürnberg (FAU), Erlangen, Germany, 2 Adidas AG, Future Sport Science, Herzogenaurach, Germany, 3 Adidas AG,\nTechnology & Innovation, Herzogenaurach, Germany, 4 Runtastic GmbH, Pasching, Austria, 5 Institute for Applied Public\nHealth and Exercise Medicine, Furtwangen University (HFU), Furtwangen, Germany\nObjective: Finishing a marathon requires to prepare for a 42.2 km run. Current literature\ndescribes which training characteristics are related to marathon performance. However,\nwhich training is most effective in terms of a performance improvement remains unclear.\nMethods: W", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "od prior to an absolved marathon. The analysis was performed on\nunsupervised ﬁtness app data (Runtastic) from 6,771 marathon ﬁnishers. Differences in\ntraining volume and intensity between three response and three marathon performance\ngroups were anal"}
{"chunk_id": "train_app_data_marathon_2021_p0001_c0009", "source_registry_id": "src_cc72f1165e30", "section_anchor": "d54f4dae1d15", "paragraph_hash": "a9cdd0ec86f62eef", "text_span_hash": "a9cdd0ec86f62eef", "source_file": "train_app_data_marathon_2021.pdf", "source_path": "C:\\Users\\26318\\Documents\\trae_projects\\ollama_pro\\马拉松助手\\data\\domain_docs\\train_app_data_marathon_2021.pdf", "page": 1, "section": "fixed_window", "paragraph_index": 9, "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "text_span": "n performance\ngroups were analyzed. Training response was quantiﬁed by the improvement of the\nvelocity of 10 km runs 1v10 between the ﬁrst and last 4 weeks of the training period.\nResponse and marathon performance groups were classiﬁed by the 33.3rd", "chunking_strategy": "fixed_window", "parent_text": "Frontiers in Physiology | www.frontiersin.org\nMay 2021 | Volume 12 | Article 669884\nPantelis Theodoros Nikolaidis,\nUniversity of West Attica, Greece\nSingidunum University, Serbia\nUniversity College Dublin, Ireland\nNortheastern University, United States\nmarkus.zrenner@fau.de\nThis article was submitted to\nExercise Physiology,\na section of the journal\nFrontiers in Physiology\nZrenner M, Heyde C, Duemler B,\nDykman S, Roecker K and\nEskoﬁer BM (2021) Retrospective\nAnalysis of Training and Its Response\nin Marathon Finishers Based on\nRetrospective Analysis of Training\nand Its Response in Marathon\nFinishers Based on Fitness App Data\nMarkus Zrenner 1*, Christian Heyde 2, Burkhard Duemler 3, Solms Dykman 4, Kai Roecker 5\nand Bjoern M. Eskoﬁer 1\n1 Machine Learning and Data Analytics Lab, Department Artiﬁcial Intelligence in Biomedical Engineering, University of\nErlangen-Nürnberg (FAU), Erlangen, Germany, 2 Adidas AG, Future Sport Science, Herzogenaurach, Germany, 3 Adidas AG,\nTechnology & Innovation, Herzogenaurach, Germany, 4 Runtastic GmbH, Pasching, Austria, 5 Institute for Applied Public\nHealth and Exercise Medicine, Furtwangen University (HFU), Furtwangen, Germany\nObjective: Finishing a marathon requires to prepare for a 42.2 km run. Current literature\ndescribes which training characteristics are related to marathon performance. However,\nwhich training is most effective in terms of a performance improvement remains unclear.\nMethods: W", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "n performance\ngroups were analyzed. Training response was quantiﬁed by the improvement of the\nvelocity of 10 km runs 1v10 between the ﬁrst and last 4 weeks of the training period.\nResponse and marathon performance groups were classiﬁed by the 33.3rd"}
