ieve that the higher\nportion was due to the unsupervised nature of the data as well\nas the low threshold of > 0.8 · hrmax we set to verify the best\n10 km performances. However, increasing the threshold of hrmax\nto elevate the cardiopulmonary eﬀort for the best 10 km velocities\ndid no", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "other unsupervised investigations (Leyk et al.,\n2009; Smyth and Muniz-Pumares, 2020). Lower training volumes\nmight be caused by the heterogeneous nature of the larger data\n4.2. Evaluation of Response Groups\nWe introduced an approach to assess physic"}
