ining period up to ﬁnal average marathon\nvelocity and high velocity runs (> 1.2 · vmp) not accounting for\nmore than 5% of the overall training volume was associated with\na higher 1v10 which likely beneﬁted the marathon performance\nas well. We also demonstrated that a high training vo", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "associated with\na higher 1v10 which likely beneﬁted the marathon performance\nas well. We also demonstrated that a high training volume does\nnot generally inﬂuence the response to training.\nThe large variances in both the training characteristics and"}
