ining period up to ﬁnal average marathon\nvelocity and high velocity runs (> 1.2 · vmp) not accounting for\nmore than 5% of the overall training volume was associated with\na higher 1v10 which likely beneﬁted the marathon performance\nas well. We also demonstrated that a high training vo", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "training characteristics and\nthe corresponding responses indicate that the most eﬀective\ntraining plan for an individual has yet to be developed. However,\ncoaches and athletes also have to acknowledge that, even with the\nbest and most eﬀective train"}
