raining period up to ﬁnal average marathon\nvelocity and high velocity runs (> 1.2 · vmp) not accounting for\nmore than 5% of the overall training volume was associated with\na higher 1v10 which likely beneﬁted the marathon performance\nas well. We also demonstrated that a high training vo", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "t\npreferences: evidence from marathon runners. Manage. Sci. 63, 1657–1672.\nAltini, M., and Amft, O. (2018). “Estimating running performance combining non-\ninvasive physiological measurements and training patterns in free-living,” in\n40th Annual Inter"}
