raining period up to ﬁnal average marathon\nvelocity and high velocity runs (> 1.2 · vmp) not accounting for\nmore than 5% of the overall training volume was associated with\na higher 1v10 which likely beneﬁted the marathon performance\nas well. We also demonstrated that a high training vo", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "-living,” in\n40th Annual International Conference of the IEEE Engineering in Medicine and\nBerndsen, J., Smyth, B., and Lawlor, A. (2020). “Mining marathon training\ndata to generate useful user proﬁles,” in International Workshop on Machine\nLearning a"}
