aining period up to ﬁnal average marathon\nvelocity and high velocity runs (> 1.2 · vmp) not accounting for\nmore than 5% of the overall training volume was associated with\na higher 1v10 which likely beneﬁted the marathon performance\nas well. We also demonstrated that a high training vo", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "Workshop on Machine\nLearning and Data Mining for Sports Analytics (Cham: Springer), 113–125.\nBillat, V. L., Demarle, A., Slawinski, J., Paiva, M., and Koralsztein, J.-P. (2001).\nPhysical and training characteristics of top-class marathon runners. Med"}
