tensities can be categorized into\nthree zones delineated by two lactate/ventilation thresholds:\nlow- (LI), moderate- (MI), and high-intensity (HI) zones.\nWhen compared to other zones, low-intensity exercises do\nnot significantly challenge the cardiopulmonary system,\nd", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "0% of) maximal norms. Despite research indicating the rel-\nevance of high-intensity training in athletes (Midgley et al.\n2006; Wen et al. 2019; Odden et al. 2024), goal-oriented\nathletes seem to almost universally prioritize the volume of\nlow-, and n"}
