nintense MI and HI exercises, genetics, and sufficient nutri-\ntion and rest cannot be ruled out.\nThis ‘structural hypothesis’ is not a new proposition.\nSome of the leading experts have also suggested LI training\nto predispose athletes to peripheral and even subtle central\n", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "in cross-\ncountry skiers after several years of training (Rusko 1992).\nCompared to fast-twitch fibers, slow-twitch ones are\nmore economical (Krustrup et al. 2008), so a gradual\nincrease in their proportion may play a role in the gradual\nimprovement"}
