rol, the volume of LI training could be\ndramatically reduced and replaced by higher-intensity train-\ning. A concern with this approach is the increased risk of\novertraining syndrome and a higher injury rate.\nWhile overtraining syndrome may be witnessed in the\nfield, very li", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "ining a high total volume of low-intensity physical\nactivity with HI training appears to be more effective than\nHI training alone in untrained (Burton et al. 2021) and\nmoderately trained individuals (Hautala et al. 2012). The\nhypothesis in this conte"}
