ntrol, the volume of LI training could be\ndramatically reduced and replaced by higher-intensity train-\ning. A concern with this approach is the increased risk of\novertraining syndrome and a higher injury rate.\nWhile overtraining syndrome may be witnessed in the\nfield, very li", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "fter all. Carefully\nplanned intensified training could be an equally feasible\ntraining method as traditional methods incorporating a\nhigh volume of LI training.\nShould LI training turn out to be replaceable by more\nintensified training, it would sugg"}
