trol, the volume of LI training could be\ndramatically reduced and replaced by higher-intensity train-\ning. A concern with this approach is the increased risk of\novertraining syndrome and a higher injury rate.\nWhile overtraining syndrome may be witnessed in the\nfield, very li", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "sified training, it would suggest that top-level athletic\nperformance depends not on the large volume of LI train-\ning, but rather on a large volume of endurance training,\nregardless of intensity.\nHigh training volume itself, typically accumulated th"}
