e-\nmatched controls resulting in a 51% lower mean 10 years FRS\nA CAC Score ≥ 100 was found in 36% of runners, generally suggesting\nan underestimation of cardiovascular risk in asymptomatic runners\nAge 43 (IQR 39–48) years\nImpact of ultra-marathon and marathon on biomarkers of myocyte necrosi", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "an\nvalues at 432 U/L (112–705) and cTnT elevation with median values at 0.036\n(0.011–0.225) compared to baseline values\nAge 44.7 ± 9.2 years\nInfluence of marathon running on plasma levels of ANP\nAfter the marathon race, a 1.8-fold increase in proANP"}
