ls after 2–7 days of recovery\nAge 37 ± 2.1 years\nAssociation between hematological parameters and iron metabolism response\nafter a marathon race\nAfter the marathon, no changes in erythrocytes, Hb, Hct, MCV and MCH\nIron increased by 1.1-fold, ferritin by 1.3-fold immediately after the race\nE", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "and in 28.0% of female athletes\nFunctional iron deficiency was present in 3.9% of male and 25.5% of female\nBody iron stores calculated by TSAT/ferritin ratio were significantly higher in male\nathletes compared to female runners\nIron overload was fou"}
