no changes in erythrocytes, Hb, Hct, MCV and MCH\nIron increased by 1.1-fold, ferritin by 1.3-fold immediately after the race\nE", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "runners\nIron overload was found in 15.0% of male but only in 4.7% of female runners"}
