aches val-\nues up to 115 l∙min−1, corresponding to a 15-fold increase\ncompared to rest [39, 126]. Lung function is significantly\nbetter in marathon runners compared to sedentary con-\ntrols [127]. Significantly higher volumes of forced expira-\ntory volume in 1 s (FEV1), forced vital capacity ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "nd in nonelite marathon run-\nners compared to sedentary controls (see Table 4) [127].\nAdditionally, recreational runners could improve their\nlung function, i.e., FVC and FEV1 over a 2-year train-\ning period [128]. Even older runners (range 40–75 year"}
