, changes\nin pulmonary function after a marathon race are most\nlikely explained by a combination of airway obstruction,\nrestriction, as well as respiratory muscle fatigue [12].\nAsthma and Atopy in Marathon Runners\nDespite positive effects of endurance training on lung\nvolumes and airway respon", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "bulin\n(Ig) E response for one or more selected allergens (see\nTable 4) [135, 136]. In this regard, some authors sus-\npect typical upper respiratory tract infections (URTIs)\nafter a marathon to be of allergic or autoimmune origin\nrather than infectiou"}
