ed\n1.1–1.3-fold lower maximal heart rate values compared to the control group\nsuggesting significantly lower cardiorespiratory fitness\nNo significant within-group differences in serum creatinine, urinary creatinine\nexcretion rate and changes in albuminuria across time in any of the gr", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "isease, eGFR estimated glomerular filtration rate, IQR interquartile range, NSAID non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs, 95% CI 95% confidence interval\nIntervention/Observation\nPhysical activity and change in estimated GFR in chronic kidney disease ("}
