te exercise, which makes physical activity\nsafe for cirrhotic patients, and positive effects outweigh\npossible negative consequences in the long term [14]. A\nrecent meta-analysis (see Table 9) investigating the risk\nof hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) in physically active\nsubjects found that great", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "cinoma, OR odds\nratio, RIPC remote ischemic preconditioning, 95% CI 95% confidence interval\nIntervention/Observation\nEffects of endurance exercise in obese patients\nwith fatty liver disease\nPhysical activity led to a marked reduction of intra-\nas wel"}
