lure [10, 202]. These patients were criti-\ncally ill and often needed liver transplantation in ~ 30% of\ncases [202]. Some patients responded reasonably well to\nconservative treatment, but mortality in patients present-\ning with acute liver failure after a marathon must not be\nunderestimated as", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "tress [36]. Mara-\nthon training and running influence the musculoskeletal\nsystem to a great extent in both a positive (e.g., increased\nbone mineral density) and a negative way (e.g., running-\nrelated injuries) [15, 54]. The impact of endurance exer-"}
