ilure [10, 202]. These patients were criti-\ncally ill and often needed liver transplantation in ~ 30% of\ncases [202]. Some patients responded reasonably well to\nconservative treatment, but mortality in patients present-\ning with acute liver failure after a marathon must not be\nunderestimated as", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "The impact of endurance exer-\ncise on the function of the musculoskeletal system has\nbeen greatly researched over the past decades. In this\ncontext, we identified 66 studies examining the positive\nas well as harmful influences of marathon training an"}
