ailure [10, 202]. These patients were criti-\ncally ill and often needed liver transplantation in ~ 30% of\ncases [202]. Some patients responded reasonably well to\nconservative treatment, but mortality in patients present-\ning with acute liver failure after a marathon must not be\nunderestimated as", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "uences of marathon training and\nrunning on the musculoskeletal system. In Table 5, the\nkey aspects of said studies are depicted.\nImpact on Bone Health\nMarathon training and running greatly impact the mus-\nculoskeletal system. Bone health is especiall"}
