nzymes\n[215, 217]. Early studies performed muscle biopsies in\nmarathon runners and found an increased mitochondria\ncount, more myoglobin, and a higher capillary density\nwhich in turn leads to an improved oxygen extraction\nfrom the blood and a more efficient energy metabolism\nsuch as an improv", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "ara-\nthon training and running on osteoarthritis in elite and\nrecreational runners [15, 220–223]. An MRI study of\nrecreational marathon runners found transient changes\nin meniscal signal alterations, whereas no harmful long-\nterm effects of marathon"}
