ces on running performance or health,\nAlterations in Iron Metabolism and Runner’s Anemia\nIron is an important component of hemoglobin, essential\nfor oxygen transport and therefore of great importance\nfor endurance exercise [276]. A marathon race leads to\nseveral alterations in biomarkers of ir", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": ", iron deficiency was present in 16–28% of\nathletes [276, 277] whereas < 2% of male runners were\nfound with iron deficiency [276]. Approximately 50% of\nfemale and male runners with iron deficiency were ane-\nmic [276]. Runner’s anemia is a much-discus"}
