ces on running performance or health,\nAlterations in Iron Metabolism and Runner’s Anemia\nIron is an important component of hemoglobin, essential\nfor oxygen transport and therefore of great importance\nfor endurance exercise [276]. A marathon race leads to\nseveral alterations in biomarkers of ir", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "nner’s anemia is a much-discussed topic\nwith very contentious data [278]. Based on the data that\niron deficiency is a common occurrence in endurance\nsports, some authors postulate that runner’s anemia is\ndue to iron deficiency [278]. Nonetheless, onl"}
