ces on running performance or health,\nAlterations in Iron Metabolism and Runner’s Anemia\nIron is an important component of hemoglobin, essential\nfor oxygen transport and therefore of great importance\nfor endurance exercise [276]. A marathon race leads to\nseveral alterations in biomarkers of ir", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "ciency [278]. Nonetheless, only a fraction\nof runners with iron deficiency have anemia [276–278].\nOther authors suggest changes in erythrocyte volume as\nthe cause of anemia [36]. Marathon running, particularly\nthrough training, increases plasma volum"}
