ct of exercise [16, 315]. The\nreason for this is probably myokines, which are released\nmore frequently and thus promote the release of anti-\ninflammatory cytokines such as IL-10 [16, 315]. This is of\nparticular interest as high baseline CRP levels are associ-\nated with an increased risk of de", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "s on the immune system and its func-\ntion [17, 317]. A study found a decreased DNA resistance\nto oxidative damage after a marathon race [316]. Due to\nthe increased metabolism, especially by skeletal muscle\ncells or activation of phagocytes as part of"}
