unction. These consequences are often not\nvery dramatic, making marathon training and running all\nin all safe for the immune system.\nMarathon running greatly influences the balance of the\ntightly regulated endocrine system. Usually, the hypotha-\nlamic-pituitary axis is affected and altered by ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "ction [57, 325]. In this regard, an acute\nelevation of growth hormone (GH) after a marathon\nrun (see Table 11) has been observed in different stud-\nies [325, 326]. Presumably, GH alters metabolic pathways\nin such a way that is beneficial for the body"}
