volume, frequency, duration of taper, and type of taper [1,14]. Most of the studies\nconfirm that their designed pre-competition tapering strategies could improve sports perfor-\nmance [15–18]. However, researchers disagree on which variables and how much to change.\nJafer", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "duration of\n8–14-day taper [22], but some have used that a shorter (\u0014 7 days) [23] or longer (> 28 days)\nletic competitions. In addition, the types of tapering including step and progressive tapers\nhave been proven effective [25], however, the progr"}
