e, frequency, duration of taper, and type of taper [1,14]. Most of the studies\nconfirm that their designed pre-competition tapering strategies could improve sports perfor-\nmance [15–18]. However, researchers disagree on which variables and how much to change.\nJafer", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "ctive [25], however, the progressive taper appears to be more successful\n[26]. In summary, pre-competition tapering methods in the aforementioned studies differ sig-\nnificantly, and it is still unclear about which tapering are better at improving the"}
