24). Recent years have\nwitnessed a deepening examination of this topic, resulting in more\ndetailed classification schemes. The Norwegian Olympic Committee\n(NOC) adopted a six-zone intensity model for elite endurance\nathletes (Tønnessen et al., 2024) and clas", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "orwegian Olympic Committee\n(NOC) adopted a six-zone intensity model for elite endurance\nathletes (Tønnessen et al., 2024) and classifies Zones 1 and 2 (Z1,\nZ2) as low-intensity effort, Zone 3 (Z3) as moderate intensity, and\nZones 4 to 6 (Z4–Z6) as hi"}
