ion and refinement\nof the latter. Both are relevant for the meticulous regulation of\ntraining programs and the precise management of training load\nThe three-zone concept has been successfully improved by the\nmany training zone classification t", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "ience advances (Figure 3).\nThe development of training intensity distribution (TID) has\nprogressed over decades. The lactate threshold model (THR)\nwas first introduced in the 1970s (Kindermann et al., 1979),\nFrontiers in Physiology"}
