y for improving\nendurance, places a strong emphasis on training inside the\ndesignated “golden intensity zone” of endurance training. Its\ntraining advantages and the physiological adaptation have garnered\ncontinuous scrutiny and have been fully corroborated for the", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "cross-country skiers frequently adopt PYR\npatterns during high-volume training phases, highlighting its role\nin sports with prolonged submaximal demands.\n3.2.3 Relative limitations\nSimilarly, there are certain limitations with the lactate threshold"}
