ies, including the pyramidal model, lactate threshold model,\nand polarized model, in the middle of the 20th century has\nsparked continuous debate about which model improves endurance\nperformance more universally and effectively in both academic and\npractical contexts", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "sive applicability, training science advancements\nindicate an increasing trend towards transitioning from pyramidal\nto polarized structures, especially in cyclic endurance sports\ncharacterized by high training volumes (Table 8).\nChampions of the pola"}
