ies, including the pyramidal model, lactate threshold model,\nand polarized model, in the middle of the 20th century has\nsparked continuous debate about which model improves endurance\nperformance more universally and effectively in both academic and\npractical contexts", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "aining load is measured: the distribution frequently\nappears polarized (with Zone 1 representing 75% and Zone\n3 approximately 17%) when training sessions are assessed by\nfrequency (like per session), but when evaluated by training time\nor distance, t"}
