mixed with periods of slower running. The pacing variations\nare determined by the athlete’s feelings and rhythms and terrain\nProgressive long runs\nA commonly used training form used by African runners. The first part of the session\nis identical to an easy long run. After about half the distance, the pace grad", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["training_protocol"], "text": "(6 × 400 m) with 30–60 s and\n2–3 min. recovery between intervals and sets, respectively. Recommended total time\nfor elite runners is ~ 15–20 min\nLactate tolerance training\nIntervals typically ranging from 200 to 600 m with 800–1500 m race pace and 1"}
